    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/382": {
      "title": "WS - KYCO Tutor",
      "description": "WS - KYCO Tutor. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. KYCO TUTOR Division: KYCO Department: Student Affairs Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSKYCOTUTOR Supervisor/Reports To: Tiffany Coleman Start Date: 8/1/2025 Provide tutoring support to KYCO students in designated course content areas. Encourage academic success through effective communication, structured study support, and collaboration with faculty. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Provide individual tutoring sessions in approved subjects – C, CT, T Guide and support students in becoming more successful, independent learners – C, P, CTR Help students master course concepts and applications under direction of the course director – CT, C Integrate effective study strategies and promote academic success – CT, P Encourage systematic approaches to studying – C, CSD Use effective and respectful communication skills with diverse individuals – C, CTR, P Maintain consistent communication with supervisor and tutoring coordinator – C, TW, L Abide by FERPA regulations and uphold confidentiality at all times – P Demonstrate clear and effective communication – C Utilize organized note-taking and academic documentation – T, C Establish positive relationships with students, faculty, and staff – TW, CTR Participate in offered professional development – CSD, P Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self-Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Education Requirements: Must be a current KYCO student with a minimum grade of 'B' in the course(s) to be tutored. Preferred Skills: Strong note-taking, effective communication, professionalism, and tutoring or mentoring experience. Work Schedule: No more than 5 hours per week unless otherwise approved. Work Conditions: Indoor environment under normal office/study room conditions. Physical Demands: Keyboarding and extended periods of seated work. Number of Positions: Varies Pay Rate: $15.00/hour Location: HPE Building To Apply: Upload your application and resume, and submit an unofficial transcript to show course competence. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/383": {
      "title": "WS - KYCO Classroom IT/AV Liaison",
      "description": "WS - KYCO Classroom IT/AV Liaison. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. KYCO CLASSROOM IT/AV LIAISON Division: KYCO Department: IT AV Experience: Entry-level Job Code: IWSKYCOITAV Supervisor/Reports To: Teddy Murphy Start Date: 8/25/2025 The Classroom IT/AV Liaison assists KYCOM faculty with the effective use of educational technology during class sessions. They ensure all classroom tech—such as lecture capture, projectors, smart boards, VR systems, and Virtual Anatomy Lab computers—operates smoothly and troubleshoot issues as they arise. Acting as the primary point of contact between faculty and the IT department, this role supports uninterrupted teaching and learning activities. Assist faculty with effective use of educational technology during class sessions – P, T Participate in training on classroom and methods technology for the KYCO curriculum – T, CSD Ensure proper operation of classroom technology—including lecture capture, projectors and screens, smart boards, TV screens, camera systems, VR systems, and Virtual Anatomy Lab equipment – T, CT Troubleshoot technology issues in HPE, Booth Auditorium, and other campus classrooms as needed – T, CT Serve as liaison between KYCOM faculty and the IT department, providing guidance and support for technology-related needs – C, TW Career Competencies: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self-Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Education Requirements: Must be a current member of the KYCO class of 2024 or 2026 in good standing. Preferred Skills: Interest in technology; adept at quickly learning new software and platforms; prior troubleshooting experience; strong interpersonal and problem‑solving skills; positive, adaptable attitude. Work Schedule: Flexible around KYCOM class schedule; hours align with scheduled class sessions. Work Conditions: Classroom and methods labs across campus (HPE, Booth Auditorium, Coal Building). Physical Demands: Standing, walking, moving and setting up equipment; ability to remain calm and professional under pressure; comfortable interacting with diverse personalities. Number of Positions: 2 Pay Rate: $500/semester stipend Location: HPE Building classrooms To Apply: Submit application and resume through the UPIKE campus employment system; coordinate with Teddy Murphy for placement. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/384": {
      "title": "WS - KYCOM Classroom IT/AV Liaison",
      "description": "WS - KYCOM Classroom IT/AV Liaison. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. KYCOM CLASSROOM IT/AV LIAISON Division: KYCOM Department: IT Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSKYCOMITLIA Supervisor/Reports To: Teddy Murphy Start Date: 8/25/2025 The Classroom IT/AV Liaison trains and supports KYCOM faculty in the use of educational technology during class sessions. This role ensures lecture capture, projectors, smart boards, cameras, and other classroom equipment function correctly and provides troubleshooting as needed. Serving as the key contact between faculty and the IT department, the liaison facilitates smooth teaching and learning experiences. Assist faculty with the appropriate and effective use of educational technology during class times – P, T Participate in training on classroom and methods technology applicable to the KYCOM curriculum – T, CSD Ensure proper functioning of technology equipment including lecture capture, projectors, screens, smart boards, TV screens, camera/projector systems, and Panopto tasks – T, CT Perform daily microphone checks and manage volume levels via touch panels – C, T Troubleshoot technology issues in lecture classrooms (e.g., rooms 210, 213) and Gross Lab camera/projector setups – T, CT Serve as liaison between KYCOM faculty and IT department for technology-related guidance and support – C, TW Career Competencies: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self-Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Preferred Skills: Interest in technology; ability to learn new software quickly; prior troubleshooting experience; strong interpersonal and problem‑solving skills; positive and adaptable attitude. Work Schedule: Must attend all scheduled KYCOM class sessions; schedule aligns with class times. Work Conditions: In-person classroom environments across campus. Physical Demands: Standing, walking, setting up and moving equipment; ability to handle stressful technical issues calmly. Number of Positions: 2 Pay Rate: $500/semester stipend Location: Coal Building classrooms To Apply: Submit application and resume through the UPIKE campus employment system; coordinate with Thomas Adams for placement. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or admission of students. #LI-DNI"
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/385": {
      "title": "WS - Family & New Student Connections Content Specialist 2",
      "description": "WS - Family & New Student Connections Content Specialist 2. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. FAMILY & NEW STUDENT CONNECTIONS CONTENT SPECIALIST 2 Division: Support Services Department: Family Connections Experience: Entry Level Job Code: NA Supervisor/Reports To: Sara Coots The Family and New Student Connections Content Specialist supports the online presence and engagement for Family Connections, First‑Year Experience, and Second‑Year Experience programs. This role assists with content creation, social media management, analytics, and multimedia to inform and engage students, families, alumni, and the broader community. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Create and curate engaging content for social platforms (Facebook, X, Instagram, CampusGroups, CampusESP) – CSD, CT, CTR, T Monitor and manage department social accounts; review comments, DMs, likes, stories, and newsletters with the Director – C, P, TW Maintain a content calendar aligned to the academic calendar and audience needs – CT, L, P, T Use analytics to track engagement and reach; recommend improvements based on insights – CSD, P, T Capture and edit photos and video for multimedia posts – CTR, P, T Collaborate with departments, student orgs, and partners to promote events and initiatives – CSD, C, CTR, P, TW Maintain accurate contact lists and mailing databases – C, TW, T Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self-Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Education Requirements: Cumulative GPA of 2.5 or higher; enrolled full‑time as a student. Preferred Skills: Strong understanding of social media; excellent written & verbal communication; basic graphic design; photo/video editing; familiarity with analytics tools; collaborative and independent work; creative storytelling; openness to feedback. Work Schedule: Flexible to accommodate class schedule; must comply with university student employment hour limits. Work Conditions: Office and event environments; variable noise/light; occasional evening/weekend social coverage. Physical Demands: Keyboarding; reaching/handling; occasional lifting/carrying of media equipment up to 20 lbs. Number of Positions: 1 Start Date: 8/25/2025 Pay Rate: $9.75/hour Location: UPIKE campus, various locations To Apply: Submit application and resume through the UPIKE campus employment system. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/386": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor of Neuroanatomy",
      "description": "Open Rank Professor of Neuroanatomy. Department: KYCOM Basic Science. Full-Time. The University of Pikeville, Kentucky College of Osteopathic Medicine (KYCOM) is currently seeking qualified candidates for the position of Assistant/Associate/Professor of Neuroanatomy/Anatomy. The successful candidate will report directly to the Associate Dean for Biomedical Sciences and is responsible for teaching, scholarly activity/research and service in the basic sciences and Neuroanatomy/Anatomy. Responsibilities: Teaching Neuroanatomy and Anatomy and includes preparation of lectures, lecture notes, learning objectives, PowerPoint slides, exam questions, and syllabi. Participates in and recommends curriculum development and evaluation. Research and other scholarly activities. Provide counseling and guidance for the students. Serves on assigned KYCOM, KYCO, and the University of Pikeville committees. Attends Commencement, White Coat Ceremony, new student orientation, and University of Pikeville Opening Convocation. Participates in Faculty Development. Assists in the selection of students to attend KYCOM. Other duties as assigned by the KYCOM Dean. Education/Experience/Skill Requirements: Earned Doctorate degree. Previous academic experience preferably at an osteopathic or allopathic medical educational program. Experience teaching face-to-face and/or online within a higher education environment. Must have excellent verbal and writing communication skills. Strong critical thinking, anticipatory problem solving and attention to detail is required. Ability to plan, prioritize, and organize work to complete assignments accurately and within reasonable timeframes. Ability to embrace diversity to best serve a growing higher education community. Ability to foster excellence and innovation. A history of demonstrating strong character and outstanding integrity. Must have current knowledge and skills in utilizing Microsoft Office Applications, including but not limited to Outlook, PowerPoint, Word, and Excel. Must be able to learn and utilize Learning Management Systems such as Canvas; and the University online platform and systems. Must demonstrate cooperation, courtesy, and consideration when working with professional community, KYCOM, KYCO and UPIKE communities, faculty, students, and the public. Must be able to work independently and also as a member of a team. Alignment with the University of Pikeville, KYCOM and KYCO missions. The University of Pikeville offers a competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. UPIKE offers a competitive benefits package including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance, telemedicine, long term disability, tuition waivers, a 403(b)-retirement plan, and HSA, FSA, & dependent care accounts. UPIKE also offers a generous holiday schedule and paid leave program. Application review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 07/21/2026 will be given priority consideration. Important Notes: Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please, specifically address the qualifications, competencies and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, copies of their transcripts, a teaching philosophy statement, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/399": {
      "title": "WS - TCDM Tutor",
      "description": "WS - TCDM Tutor. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. TCDM Tutor Division: TCDM Department: TCDM Student Affairs Experience: Experienced Job Code: IWSTCDMTUTOR GL Code: Supervisor of Student Employee(s): Karen Pruett FWS, IWS, or Grant Funded: ☐ FWS, ☒ IWS, ☐ Grant Funded Avg. Hours/Week: ☒ 1-5, ☒ 6-10, ☐ 11-15, ☐ 16-20 Requested Start Date: --07/01/26 Term of Position: ☒ Summer, ☒ Fall, ☒ Spring Provide tutoring services to TCDM students in approved subjects, facilitating academic success and promoting effective study strategies. Ideal for experienced students with strong communication skills and a passion for helping peers succeed. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Guide and support students in becoming more successful, independent learners – C, P, CTR Help students master course concepts and applications under advisement of the course director – CT, C Integrate effective study strategies and promote academic success – CT, P Encourage systematic approaches to studying – C, CSD Use effective and respectful communication skills with diverse individuals – C, CTR, P Maintain consistent communication with supervisor. – C, TW, L Abide by FERPA regulations and uphold confidentiality at all times – P Demonstrate clear and effective communication – C Utilize organized note-taking and academic documentation – T, C Establish positive relationships with students, faculty, and staff – TW, CTR Participate in offered professional development – CSD, P Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Qualifications: : Must be a current KYCO & KYCOM ( with approval from Dean) or TCDM student with a minimum grade of 'B' (85%) in the course(s) to be tutor. In the following sections check all boxes that apply to your job. Computer Skills: ☐ Word, ☐ Excel, ☐ PowerPoint, ☐ Canva, ☐ Social Media & New Technology, ☐ Other: _________________________ Other Skills: ☒ Attention to detail, ☒ Strong active listening abilities, ☒ Public speaking, ☒ Written & verbal communication, ☐ Customer focused, ☒ Willingness to learn new things Work Schedule: ☐ Su ___ to ___; ☐ M ___ to ___; ☐ T ___ to ___; ☐ W ___ to ___; ☐ R ___ to ___; ☐ F ___ to ___; ☐ Sa ___ to ___; ☒ Hours vary depending on workload (Check days that apply, insert hours if set, otherwise, check “Hours vary depending on workload”.) No more than 5 hours per week unless otherwise approved Work Conditions: ☐ Heat, ☐ Cold, ☐ Odors/Smoke, ☐ Toxic Agents, ☐ Dust, ☐ Machinery, ☐ Light Intensity, ☐ Noise, ☐ Vibrations, ☐ Wetness, ☐ Humidity, ☐ Electrical Currents, ☐ Other: _________________________ Physical Demands: ☐ Keyboarding, ☐ Reaching/Handling, ☐ Stooping/Kneeling, ☐ Crouching/Crawling, ☐ Pushing up to ___ lbs., ☐ Pulling up to ___ lbs., ☐ Lifting up to ___ lbs., ☐ Carrying up to ___ lbs., ☐ Climbing, ☐ Balancing, ☐ Other: _________________________ Number of Positions: Pay Rate: $15.00/hr Location: Building: ___Sim Center__, Room #: ___N/A__ Additional Comments: Strong note-taking, effective communication, professionalism, and tutoring or mentoring experience. Demonstrates proficient hand skills while working in the lab. Preferred past dental experience Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/405": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor - Primary Care",
      "description": "Open Rank Professor - Primary Care. Department: KYCOM Family Medicine. Full-Time. The University of Pikeville seeks an innovative, energetic and collaborative candidate to assume the position of Assistant/Associate/Professor of Primary Care. This full-time position is under the supervision of the Chair of the Department of Primary Care. The position is directly responsible for teaching, osteopathic clinical research, and service in the Kentucky College of Osteopathic Medicine (KYCOM) Department of Primary Care. Approximately 550 medical students, 30 full-time faculty, and a variety of clinical partners are part of the KYCOM team. The Kentucky College of Osteopathic Medicine (KYCOM) is ranked second among all D.O. and M.D. granting medical schools in the U.S. for graduates practicing in primary care and second for those practicing in rural areas. Since 1997, KYCOM’s guiding principle has been to educate physicians to serve underserved and rural areas, with an emphasis on primary care. Nestled in the beautiful Appalachian Mountains near a growing regional hospital, KYCOM’s graduates are well prepared to enter high-quality and rigorous graduate medical education residencies. Responsibilities: Responsible for teaching in those courses and associated labs within the KYCOM Department of Primary Care. Participates in and recommends curriculum development and evaluation. Assists in preparing course syllabi, objectives, lecture schedules, and testing procedures. Assists in preparing materials and documentation required for continued school accreditation by the American Osteopathic Association - COCA and other accrediting agencies. Actively serves on appointed KYCOM Faculty and UPIKE Committees. Provides clinical services as directed by the Department Chair and KYCOM Dean, which would be associated with primary care. Provides counseling, advising, and guidance to students. Attends Commencement, White Coat Ceremony, new student orientation, and University of Pikeville Opening Convocation. Participates in Faculty Development. Assists in the selection of students to attend KYCOM. Responsible for other duties as directed by the Chair or KYCOM Dean. Education/Credentials: Must have earned a D.O. degree from a COCA-accredited college/school of osteopathic medicine. Must be board-certified by the American Osteopathic Association or American Board of Medical Specialties in a primary care specialty (Family Medicine, Internal Medicine, or Pediatrics). Current and unrestricted medical license issued by the Kentucky Board of Medical License (KBML). Current and unrestricted DEA certificate. Experience: Teaching in an academic setting is preferred. Clinical experience within a primary care setting is required. Skills and Abilities: Must have excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to embrace diversity to best serve a growing higher education community. Ability to foster excellence and innovation. A history of demonstrating strong character and outstanding integrity. Ability to plan, prioritize, and organize work to complete assignments accurately and within reasonable timeframes. Must have current knowledge and skills in utilizing Microsoft Office Applications, including but not limited to Outlook, PowerPoint, Word, and Excel. Must be able to learn and utilize Learning Management Systems such as Canvas and the University's online platform and systems. Must demonstrate cooperation, courtesy, and consideration when working with the professional community, KYCOM, KYCO, and UPIKE communities, faculty, students, and the public. Must be able to work independently and as a member of a team. Alignment with the University of Pikeville and KYCOM missions. The University of Pikeville offers a competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. UPIKE offers a competitive benefits package including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance, telemedicine, long-term disability, tuition waivers, a 403(b)-retirement plan, and HSA, FSA, and dependent care accounts. UPIKE also offers a generous holiday schedule and paid leave program. Application review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 08/16/2026 will be given priority consideration. Important Notes: Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please, specifically address the qualifications, competencies and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, copies of their transcripts, a teaching philosophy statement, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/412": {
      "title": "WS - Softball Field Worker - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Softball Field Worker - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. FIELD WORKER (STAGGS) Division: Athletics Department: Softball Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSSTBLFLDWRK Supervisor/Reports To: Robert Staggs Start Date: 8/25/2026 Support field maintenance for the UPIKE softball program including general upkeep, cleaning, and facility preparation. Ideal for students who enjoy outdoor work and want to contribute to athletic operations. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Cutting grass – C, TW, P Weed-eating – C, TW, P Working on the infield – C, TW, CT, P Cleaning the dugouts – P, C, TW Picking up trash – P, TW General field maintenance – C, TW, CT, P Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Preferred Skills: Attention to detail, strong active listening abilities, willingness to learn new things. Work Schedule: Sunday: Closed; Monday–Saturday: Varies depending on workload. Flexible to accommodate student schedules. Work Conditions: Heat, cold, noise, vibrations, wetness, humidity, dust, machinery. Physical Demands: Reaching/handling, stooping/kneeling, crouching/crawling, pushing/lifting/carrying up to 50 lbs., climbing, balancing. Number of Positions: 2 (average of 10 hours a week) Pay Rate: $8.75/hour Location: Campus softball field To Apply: Complete required sections and upload your academic schedule (and practice schedule), along with your resume. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/414": {
      "title": "WS - Museum Assistant - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Museum Assistant - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. MUSEUM ASSISTANT Division: Community Service Department: Community Service Experience: Entry-level Supervisor/Reports To: Brandon R. Kirk Start Date: 8/25/20256 The Museum Assistant supports daily operations at the Big Sandy Heritage Center Museum through visitor services, exhibition support, and administrative tasks. Working across the front desk, gift shop, and exhibit installations, the role helps deliver a welcoming, informative visitor experience while maintaining collection care and general museum upkeep. Responsibilities and Career Competencies Ensure a welcoming and informative environment for all visitors – C, TW, P, CSD, CT, CTR, L, T Handle admissions, assist with the museum gift shop, and manage cash transactions – C, TW, P, CSD, CT, CTR, L, T Assist with the care and maintenance of the museum collection – C, TW, P, CSD, CT, CTR, L, T Lead and assist with sorting, arranging, cataloging, and inventorying artifacts, rare documents, and photographs – C, TW, P, CSD, CT, CTR, L, T Conduct research online and in libraries on topics related to the museum mission and its collection – C, TW, P, CSD, CT, CTR, L, T Assist with the installation, maintenance, and de-installation of exhibits – C, TW, P, CSD, CT, CTR, L, T Help with the arrangement and display of artifacts – C, TW, P, CSD, CT, CTR, L, T Contribute to developing ideas and strategies for community programming – C, TW, P, CSD, CT, CTR, L, T Improve the museum’s online presence (website, Wikipedia, YouTube, social media) – C, TW, P, CSD, CT, CTR, L, T Perform routine cleaning and general maintenance of museum spaces – C, TW, P, CSD, CT, CTR, L, T Assist with events, programs, and workshops – C, TW, P, CSD, CT, CTR, L, T Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self-Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Education Requirements: Must be a current UPIKE student in good standing. Preferred Skills: Word, Social Media & New Technology; attention to detail; written & verbal communication; willingness to learn new things. Work Schedule: M 10:00 AM–4:00 PM; R 10:00 AM–4:00 PM; F 10:00 AM–4:00 PM; Sa 10:00 AM–4:00 PM (considering opening Tu & W 10:00 AM–4:00 PM; museum staff on hand until 6:00 PM M, R–Sa). Work Conditions: Dust. Physical Demands: Keyboarding; reaching/handling; stooping/kneeling; crouching/crawling; lifting and carrying up to 15 lbs.; balancing. Number of Positions: 3 Pay Rate: $8.75/hour Location: Off-campus, approximately 3 blocks from the city parking building, city park, and UPIKE. 172 Division St. 4th floor, Pikeville To Apply: Submit application and resume through the UPIKE campus employment system. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/415": {
      "title": "WS - BearWear Accounting Specialist",
      "description": "WS - BearWear Accounting Specialist. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. BEARWEAR ACCOUNTING SPECIALIST Division: CCOB Department: BearWear Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSBWACTSPL Supervisor/Reports To: Sherri Little Start Date: 8/25/2025 Support BearWear operations through processing customer orders, managing invoices, and maintaining inventory records. Ideal for students interested in accounting, customer service, and learning basic financial processes. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Processing of customer order forms – CSD, CT, TW Recording Accounts Payable invoices for ordered materials – CSD, CT, T Initiating customer invoices after delivery – C, P, CSD, CT, T Review profit/loss of orders – CSD, CT, T Develop and maintain inventory of current materials – C, TW, P, CT, T Learn the importance of documenting financial records – C, TW, P, CSD, CT, T Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Preferred Skills: Attention to detail, strong active listening abilities, written & verbal communication, customer focused. Computer Skills: Word, Excel, Social Media & New Technology Work Schedule: Monday through Friday, hours vary according to workload. Work Conditions: Heat, cold, noise. Physical Demands: Keyboarding, reaching/handling, stooping/kneeling, pushing/pulling/lifting/carrying up to 10 lbs. Mostly seated at a desk with occasional walking to other buildings. Number of Positions: 1 Pay Rate: $8.75/hour Location: Coleman College of Business, Academy Building To Apply: Complete required sections of the application, upload resume and class/practice schedule. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/416": {
      "title": "WS - Library Student Assistant",
      "description": "WS - Library Student Assistant. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. LIBRARY STUDENT ASSISTANT Division: Support Services Department: Library Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSLIBRASTI Supervisor/Reports To: Danielle Adams Start Date: 8/25/2025 Assist with circulation desk operations, customer service, and general library maintenance tasks. This position is ideal for students interested in gaining experience in a library setting with no prior experience required. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Provide high-quality customer service to meet patron's needs – C, P, TW, CTR Check in/out library materials – P, CSD, T Ensure the integrity, privacy, and confidentiality of patron records and transactions – P, CT Answer the phone and relay questions to appropriate staff when necessary – C, TW Assist library users with basic reference, resource, and technology questions – C, T, CT Help patrons locate items through familiarity with the library layout – C, P, TW Explain library policies such as reserves, printing, and computer use – C, P, CT Provide basic technology support including Canvas, email, and office software – T, C, CT Assist with copiers, printers, and library equipment – T, P Answer library-related and campus-wide directional/informational questions – C, TW, P Shelve and shift materials accurately – CSD, CT, P Clean shelves and maintain assigned areas – P, TW Conduct shelf reading for collection inventory – CT, P, CSD Perform additional tasks as assigned – TW, P, CSD Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Preferred Skills: Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, willingness to learn new technology such as 3D Printers, Cricut, Camcorders, etc., attention to detail, active listening, public speaking, written & verbal communication, customer-focused, willingness to learn. Work Schedule: Day shift and Evening shift available. Hours can be flexible to accommodate the student’s class and extracurricular schedule. Work Conditions: Dust/mold. Physical Demands: Keyboarding, reaching/handling, stooping/kneeling, crouching/crawling, pushing/pulling up to 75 lbs., lifting/carrying up to 30 lbs., climbing, balancing. Additional Notes: This role is for students interested in library environments. Training and meetings are required. Must adhere to library policies and be punctual, detail-oriented, and able to follow instructions. Number of Positions: 15 Pay Rate: $8.75/hour Location: Allara Library To Apply: Complete required sections and upload your academic and practice schedule, along with your resume or student employment application. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
