    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/417": {
      "title": "WS - Library Student Assistant II",
      "description": "WS - Library Student Assistant II. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. LIBRARY STUDENT ASSISTANT II Division: Support Services Department: Library Experience: Intermediate Job Code: FWSLIBRASTII Supervisor/Reports To: Danielle Adams Start Date: 8/25/2025 Support library operations with a focus on circulation, customer service, and technical assistance. This position is for returning student workers who have prior experience and training in Allara Library. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Provide high-quality customer service to meet patron needs – C, P, TW, CTR Check in/out library materials – T, P, CSD Ensure the integrity, privacy, and confidentiality of patron records and transactions – P, CT Answer the phone and relay questions to appropriate staff – C, TW Assist patrons with reference, resource, and technology questions – C, T, CT Help users locate library materials and explain policies – C, TW, P Provide technology support (Canvas, email, office software) – T, C, CT Assist with library equipment, printers, and copiers – T, P Answer library-related and campus-wide informational questions – C, TW, P Shelve, shift, and clean library materials – CSD, CT, P Conduct shelf reading for inventory – CT, P, CSD Perform additional tasks as assigned – TW, P, CSD Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Preferred Skills: Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Social Media & New Technology, attention to detail, active listening, public speaking, written & verbal communication, customer-focused, willingness to learn. Work Schedule: Sunday: 3:00 PM – 11:00 PM; Monday–Thursday: 7:30 AM – 12:00 AM; Friday: 7:30 AM – 5:00 PM; Saturday: 9:00 AM – 5:00 PM. Flexible with class schedule. Work Conditions: Dust. Physical Demands: Keyboarding, reaching/handling, stooping/kneeling, crouching/crawling, pushing/pulling up to 75 lbs., lifting/carrying up to 30 lbs., climbing, balancing. Additional Notes: This position builds upon prior training and experience at Allara Library. Returning students should be detail-oriented, able to follow instructions, and committed to excellent customer service. Schedules are based on class and extracurricular availability. Number of Positions: 12 Pay Rate: $9.75/hour Location: Allara Library To Apply: Complete required sections and upload your academic and practice schedule, along with your resume or student employment application. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
