    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/428": {
      "title": "WS - KYCOM Student Ambassador - IWS",
      "description": "WS - KYCOM Student Ambassador - IWS. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. KYCOM Admissions Liaison - IWS Division: KYCOM Department: Admissions Experience: Entry-level Job Code: I WSKYCOMADMLI Supervisor/Reports To: Jennifer Lockhart/David Osborne Start Date: 8/24/2026 The KYCOM Admissions Liaison facilitates prospective student engagement by conducting on-campus tours and hosting virtual Q&A sessions. Working closely with the Director of Medical School Admission, the liaison ensures prospective students receive accurate information and positive experiences. This role supports recruitment efforts through effective communication and collaboration. Conduct on-campus tours of KYCOM and UPIKE campus – C, TW Facilitate Zoom virtual question-and-answer sessions for prospective students – C, T Assist with orientation and answering emails - C, TW, P, CTR, L Use effective, respectful, and positive communication skills with diverse students, faculty, and staff – C, P Maintain regular, ongoing communication with the Director of Medical School Admission and collaborate to guide prospective students – C, TW Quickly establish positive relationships with diverse students, faculty, and staff – TW, C Perform other duties as assigned – CT Career Competencies: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self-Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Education Requirements: Must be a current KYCOM student in good academic standing. Preferred Skills: Attention to detail; customer-focused approach; self-motivated and passionate; determination to provide exceptional service; supportive of the University's mission. Work Schedule: Varies depending on student availability; includes evening and weekend hours. Work Conditions: Heat; cold; odors/smoke; noise; wetness; humidity. Physical Demands: Walking and standing for long periods; ability to occasionally climb stairs. Number of Positions: 1 Pay Rate: $10.5/hour Location: KYCOM campus and virtual To Apply: Submit application and resume through the UPIKE campus employment system. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or admission of students."
