    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/454": {
      "title": "WS - Sportsplex Archery Assistant - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Sportsplex Archery Assistant - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. Sportsplex Archery Assistant Division: Athletics Department: Archery Experience: Entry-level Job Code: NA Provide front-line support for the Sportsplex Archery program by coordinating practice schedules, assisting with events, and helping maintain equipment and facilities. Deliver friendly customer service, monitor safety and proper use of spaces, and complete opening/closing and cleaning tasks. Ideal for students interested in sport operations and hands-on archery equipment experience; training provided. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Coordinate practice schedules with UPIKE teams and visiting/high-school groups. Assist with planning and supporting archery events, competitions, tournaments, and outreach. Support pro-shop operations (basic equipment checks, cleaning, organization). Learn and assist with bow tuning, minor maintenance/repairs, and arrow building (training provided). Provide welcoming customer service; greet visitors and answer basic questions. Monitor activity for safety and proper use; complete opening/closing checklists. Maintain cleanliness of ranges and storage areas. Support fundraising, sponsor outreach, and social media updates as needed. Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Other Skills : Attention to detail, willingness to learn new things. Work Schedule : Hours may very depend on workload. Work Conditions: Heat, Cold, Light Intensity Physical Demands: Stooping/Kneeling Number of Positions: 1 Hours needed per week: Varies with practices/events; evenings/weekends as required Pay Rate: $8.75/hour Supervisor of Student Employee(s): Amber Lemke / Andrew Dekowski Requested Start Date: 9/15/2026 Location: Building: Sportsplex – Archery, Room#: Additional Comments: Add additional comments for job applicants here. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
