    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/455": {
      "title": "WS - Bowling Pro Shop Assistant - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Bowling Pro Shop Assistant - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. PRO SHOP ASSISTANT Division: Athletics Department: Bowling Experience: Entry-level Job Code: NA Supervisor/Reports To: Andrew Dekowski & Amber Lemke Start Date: 8 /24/2026 Support Bowling coaches in managing the campus Pro Shop, including customer service for student‑athletes and upkeep of team equipment throughout the season. Learn day‑to‑day Pro Shop operations and assist with scheduling, preparation, and basic maintenance tasks to ensure a safe, efficient experience for all users. Coordinate with supervisors to schedule appointments with athletes; communicate clearly with peers and visitors – C, TW, P Complete assigned tasks on time and demonstrate initiative by taking ownership of unassigned work when appropriate – P, L, CSD Learn and apply new Pro Shop skills and processes; stay current with updated procedures – CSD, T, CT Troubleshoot issues quickly, propose solutions, and take responsibility for correcting mistakes – CT, P, L Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self‑Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Education Requirements: Must be a current UPIKE student in good standing. Preferred Skills: Word; Excel; attention to detail; strong active listening; customer‑focused; willingness to learn. Work Schedule: M–F; hours vary depending on workload and athlete appointments. Work Conditions: Inside. Physical Demands: Lifting up to 25 lbs; Carrying up to 25 lbs. Number of Positions: 3 To Apply: Submit application and resume through the UPIKE campus employment system. Pay Rate: $8.75/hour Location: Sports Plex – Pro Shop Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or admission of students."
