    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/461": {
      "title": "WS - Campus Engagement Crew Member",
      "description": "WS - Campus Engagement Crew Member. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. CAMPUS ENGAGEMENT CREW MEMBER Division: Support Services Department: Center for Student Engagement (CSE) Experience: Entry Level Job Code: TBD Supervisor/Reports To: Adam Llanos Start Date: 8 /24/2026 The Campus Engagement Crew Member supports campus life by officiating intramural sports, assisting with event production, and overseeing the Student Lounge. They help ensure events run smoothly, provide a welcoming presence, and maintain student spaces. This role offers hands-on experience in teamwork, leadership, and campus engagement while developing practical event management and customer service skills. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Officiate intramural games, maintaining safety, fairness, and fun – C, TW, CSD, CTR, L Assist with setup, breakdown, and equipment management for games – C, TW Keep accurate records of participation, scores, and incidents – CSD, CT, CTR Provide a welcoming and inclusive environment for all participants – TW, P, CSD, CTR Assist with the physical setup and teardown of campus events – C, TW Operate basic event technology after training (sound systems, lights, etc.) – C, TW, CT, T Provide on-site support to ensure smooth event execution – C, TW, P, CTR, L Serve as a campus ambassador, offering assistance and direction to attendees – TW, CSD, CT, L Monitor and manage the Student Lounge during scheduled hours – C, P Check out equipment and supplies; maintain cleanliness and safety – P, CTR, T Engage with students to promote upcoming programs and services – C, TW, P, L Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self-Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Education Requirements: Must be a current UPIKE student in good standing. Preferred Skills: Proficiency with Word, Canva, social media and new technology; familiarity with Connect Teams; strong active listening abilities; customer-focused; willingness to learn new things. Work Schedule: Weekly hours will range from 2 to 6, depending on event and game schedules. Student Lounge coverage will account for up to 2 of those hours weekly. Schedules are variable (day, evening, weekends) and require open communication with the supervisor to coordinate availability. Work Conditions: Heat, Cold, Noise. Physical Demands: Keyboarding; reaching/handling; stooping/kneeling; crouching/crawling; pushing up to 30 lbs; pulling up to 30 lbs; lifting up to 50 lbs. Number of Positions: 1-4 Pay Rate: $8.75/hour Location: Student Lounge, UPIKE Gym, Hoops, Off Campus Locations To Apply: Submit application and resume through the UPIKE campus employment system. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/462": {
      "title": "WS - CSE Event Production Crew Member - FWS",
      "description": "WS - CSE Event Production Crew Member - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. CSE EVENT PRODUCTION CREW MEMBER Division: Support Services Department: CSE Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSEVTPROCRWMB Supervisor/Reports To: Adam Llanos Start Date: 8/25/2026 Support the Division of Student Affairs and Event Services team in setting up and executing campus events. Gain experience in event logistics, customer service, and A/V technology while enhancing student engagement on campus. Student will oversee the student lounge when needed. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Set up and dismantle event spaces, ensuring proper arrangement of equipment, props, and materials – C, TW, CT, T Operate audiovisual equipment to support presentations and performances – CSD, CT, T Track and manage event inventory – C, TW, CT Unload equipment and set up venues including chairs, tables, and stages – C, TW, P, CT, L Provide excellent customer service to attendees and organizers – C, P, CSD, CTR, L Ensure event setup meets outlined specifications – C, TW, P, CT, CSD, L, T Communicate effectively with team and supervisors – C, TW, P, L Maintain clean and organized event environments – P, L Attend training and team meetings to enhance skills – C, TW, L Engage in problem-solving for event logistics – C, TW, P, CSD, CT, L Collaborate with event services team on planning improvements – C, TW, P, CSD, CT, L Support Student Lounge operations and engagement programming – C, TW, CTR, L, T Competencies/Skills: Career & Self-Development (CSD), Communication (C), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Professionalism (P), Teamwork (TW), Technology (T) Education Requirements: Must be enrolled and in good academic standing at UPIKE. Preferred Skills: Outstanding organization, attention to detail, interpersonal skills, multitasking, conflict management, public speaking, and willingness to learn. Work Schedule: Sunday–Saturday, flexible based on event needs. Work Conditions: Heat, cold, odors/smoke, noise, vibrations, wetness, humidity, dust, machinery, light intensity. Physical Demands: Keyboarding, stooping/kneeling, pushing/pulling up to 250 lbs, lifting/carrying up to 30 lbs. Number of Positions: 1-4 , flexible hours per week with a minimum of 2 hours overseeing the Student Lounge. Pay Rate: $8.75/hour Location: Various campus locations; Student Lounge and Center for Student Engagement, Wickham Hall To Apply: Submit required application sections, resume, and class schedule. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or admission of students."
