    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/463": {
      "title": "WS - Conference Event Service Staff",
      "description": "WS - Conference Event Service Staff. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. CONFERENCE EVENT SERVICE STAFF Division: Support Services Department: Conference and Event Services Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSCONFEVENTST Supervisor/Reports To: Kyle McCown / Charity Deel Start Date: 8/25/2026 Support the planning and execution of campus events by setting up and striking event spaces, assisting guests, and ensuring smooth operations. This active role requires strong communication skills, attention to detail, and the ability to work under pressure. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Unload equipment and set up venues including chairs, tables, and stages – C, TW, P, CT, L Work independently under the Event Coordinator’s instruction – C, TW, P, CT, CTR, CSD, L, T Ensure correct event space setup per specifications – C, TW, P, CT, CSD, L, T Adhere to event safety standards – C, TW, P, CT, CSD, L, T Provide excellent customer service to attendees – C, TW, P, CT, CTR, CSD, L, T Assist with event security duties – C, TW, P, CT, CSD, L, T Support IT and AV needs during events – C, TW, P, CT, CSD, L, T Provide information and directions to eventgoers – C, TW, P, CT, CTR, CSD, L, T Inspect and report equipment damage – C, TW, P, CT, L, T Pack up and store equipment post-event – C, TW, P, CT Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Education Requirements: Previous event setup or related experience preferred. Preferred Skills: PowerPoint, Social Media & New Technology, attention to detail, customer focus, willingness to learn, ability to work flexible hours including weekends and holidays, strong verbal and written communication, and teamwork. Work Schedule: Sunday through Saturday; hours vary based on event workload. Work Conditions: Heat, cold, odors/smoke, noise, vibrations, wetness, humidity, dust, light intensity. Physical Demands: Reaching/handling, stooping/kneeling, crouching/crawling, pushing/pulling up to 250 lbs, lifting and carrying up to 30 lbs. Number of Positions: 5 Pay Rate: $10.50/hour Location: HPE 7th Floor and event spaces across campus To Apply: Complete required sections and upload your academic schedule and resume. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/464": {
      "title": "WS - Admissions Data Communications Assistant - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Admissions Data Communications Assistant - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. Admissions Data Communications Assistant Division: Support Services Department: Admissions Experience: Entry-level Job Code: NA Supervisor of Student Employee(s): Della Abshire Requested Start Date: 8 /24/2026 The Admissions Data Communications Assistant will contribute to the development of Admissions by software systems. Their knowledge of systems like Slate and Ellucian Databases will simplify queries for admissions staff and technological needs of the department. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Support the setup, testing, and monitoring of workflows, queries, and imports within Admissions platforms (C, T, CT) Perform routine data audits to identify duplicates, errors, or incomplete records within Admissions systems (CT, T, P) Help manage digital documents and workflows in ImageNow, including scanning, indexing, and routing Admissions materials (T, P, TW) Provide technical support to Admissions staff on system features, login issues, and workflow processes (C, T, P, TW) Help pull data from Slate and Ellucian for enrollment reporting, prospect management, and application tracking (CT, T, C) Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) In the following sections check all boxes that apply to your job. Computer Skills: Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Social Media & New Technology, Image Now, Slate, Ellucian Databases Other Skills: Attention to detail, Strong Active Listening abilities, Public Speaking, Written and verbal communication, Customer focused, Willingness to learn new things. Work Schedule: Hours may vary depending on workload Monday -Friday Physical Demands: Keyboarding, Reaching/Handling, Stooping/Kneeling, Pushing up to 100lbs, Pulling up to 100lbs, Lifting up to 10lbs, Carrying up to 10lbs Number of Positions: 2 Hours needed per week: 20 Pay Rate: $8.75/hour Location: Admissions 601A Additional Comments: Add additional comments for job applicants here. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/465": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant to the Dean of Patton College of Education",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant to the Dean of Patton College of Education. Department: Education. Full-Time. The University of Pikeville is seeking qualified candidates for a full-time, administrative assistant to the Dean of the Patton College of Education (PCOE). This position provides comprehensive administrative, clerical, and operational support for the dean and serves as the primary point of contact for students, alumni, employers, faculty, staff, and community partners. Responsibilities: Provide clerical support for the educational activities of the PCOE. Schedule appointments and take messages as needed for the PCOE Dean. Prepare and file all correspondence. Organize PCOE and Teacher Education Committee Meetings by preparing agendas, sending calendar invites, and taking and dispersing meeting minutes. Properly stock and maintain organizational and teaching supplies and compile supply orders. Assist in the development of class schedules. Maintain curriculum contracts and education handbooks. Collect and file any necessary information from education students while maintaining confidentiality. Work closely with the Registrar’s Office getting students registered for appropriate classes after admission. Organize, plan, and prepare for student events or other education activities. Access, complete, and submit maintenance work orders. Assist in report preparation related to annual reports, state program reviews, or accreditation. Provide clerical support as needed for PCOE faculty or staff. Other duties as assigned. Education: Bachelor's Degree preferred. Experience: Previous Administrative Assistant experience preferred. Must have proficient written and verbal communication skills and be able to maintain confidentiality. Must have good time management and organizational skills. Must have the ability to multi-task, prioritize assignments, and meet deadlines. Must be proficient with relevant computer software programs, including Microsoft Office software (Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Outlook) as well as the Google Suite (Google Docs, Google Sheets, etc.). Must have the ability to interact with administration, faculty, staff, and students in a highly responsive and professional manner. Important Notes: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 08/21/2026 will be given priority consideration. Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please, specifically address the qualifications, competencies and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, copies of their transcripts, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/466": {
      "title": "WS - IT Help Desk Assistant",
      "description": "WS - IT Help Desk Assistant. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. IT HELP DESK ASSISTANT Division: Support Services Department: IT Services Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSITHELPDKAST Supervisor/Reports To: Brittany Mullins Start Date: 8/25/2026 Work at the IT Helpdesk to gain hands-on experience in troubleshooting, customer service, and professional communication. Ideal for students interested in IT careers and developing practical technical support skills. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Work a helpdesk ticket queue. Respond, effectively communicate, and resolve issues in a timely manner – C, TW, P Assist student body with utilizing provided IT resources – C, CT Deploy, implement, and maintain endpoint devices for faculty, staff, and students – T Work independently and function in a team environment – L, TW, P Other duties as assigned – Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Preferred Skills: Professionalism, patience, people-first attitude, willingness to learn new technologies and customer service skills, strong active listening, attention to detail, organizational skills, time management, written & verbal communication, team orientation, basic computer knowledge, Microsoft Word and Excel. Computer Skills: Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Social Media and New Technology, troubleshooting hardware and software. Work Schedule: Monday through Friday between 9am and 4pm. Work Conditions: Heat, cold, odors/smoke, toxic agents, noise, vibrations, wetness, humidity, dust, machinery, light intensity, electrical currents. Physical Demands: Keyboarding, reaching, stooping/kneeling, crouching/crawling, pushing/pulling/lifting/carrying up to 50 lbs, climbing, balancing. Number of Positions: 3–4 students (120 hours total per student; average 20 hours/week) Pay Rate: $8.75/hour Location: Armington Learning Center, Basement #009 To Apply: Complete required sections and upload your academic schedule (and practice schedule) along with your resume. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/467": {
      "title": "WS - IT Help Desk Assistant Level II",
      "description": "WS - IT Help Desk Assistant Level II. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. IT HELP DESK ASSISTANT LEVEL II Division: Support Services Department: IT Services Experience: Intermediate Job Code: FWSITHELPDKAST Supervisor/Reports To: Brittany Mullins Start Date: 8 /24/2026 Work at the IT Helpdesk to gain advanced experience in troubleshooting, customer service, and professional communication. Ideal for students interested in further developing practical technical support skills and leadership abilities. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Work a helpdesk ticket queue. Respond, effectively communicate, and resolve issues in a timely manner – C, TW, P Assist student body with utilizing provided IT resources – C, CT Deploy, implement, and maintain endpoint devices for faculty, staff, and students – T Ability to work independently and function in a team environment – L, TW, P Other duties as assigned – Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Preferred Skills: Professionalism, patience, people-first attitude, willingness to learn customer service skills and new technologies, strong active listening abilities, attention to detail, organizational skills, time management, written & verbal communication, team orientation, basic computer knowledge, Microsoft Word and Excel. Computer Skills: Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Social Media and New Technology, troubleshooting hardware and software. Work Schedule: Monday through Friday between 9am and 4pm. Work Conditions: Heat, cold, odors/smoke, toxic agents, noise, vibrations, wetness, humidity, dust, machinery, light intensity, electrical currents. Physical Demands: Keyboarding, reaching, stooping/kneeling, crouching/crawling, pushing/pulling/lifting/carrying up to 50 lbs, climbing, balancing. Number of Positions: 3–4 students (120 hours