    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/468": {
      "title": "WS - KYCOM NIH Immunology Fellow - IWS",
      "description": "WS - KYCOM NIH Immunology Fellow - IWS. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. NIH Immunology Fellow Division: KYCOM Department: Academic Affairs Experience: Entry-level Job Code: IWSKYCOMNIH Supervisor/Reports to: Malgorzata Simm Start Date : 8/15/2026 Responsibilities and Career Competencies Assist with organ harvesting from body donors in Gross Anatomy Laboratory (C, TW, CSD, P) Perform histological examination of thymic and splenic tissues (C, CSD, CT, T, P) Perform molecular biology experiments (DNA/RNA isolation and analysis) (C, CSD, CT, T) Assist with data collection and analysis (C, CSD, CT, T, TW) Track record of presentations to scientific and other audiences (P, C, CSD, CT, T, TW, L) Competencies/Skills: Communication (C) , Teamwork (TW) , Professionalism (P) , Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L),Technology (T) Qualifications: Basic laboratory training and experience, including knowledge of research techniques and methodologies; strong analytical and data visualization skills; maintain 75% average grades with no course failures Computer Skills: Excel, PowerPoint, Social Media & New Technology, Research-related Technology Other Skills: Attention to detail, Strong active listening abilities, Public speaking, Written & verbal communication, Willingness to learn new things Work Schedule: 10h/week during semester, 30h/week during summer Work Conditions: Employee encounters while performing essential functions of the job: Odors/Smoke, Toxic Agents, Noise, Vibrations Number of Positions: 1-6 Pay Rate: $25/hour Location: KYCOM Research Laboratory/ Coal Building / Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/471": {
      "title": "WS - Sports Information Assistant - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Sports Information Assistant - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. SPORTS INFORMATION ASSISTANT Division: Athletics Department: Sports Information Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSPINFOAST Supervisor/Reports To: Cheryl Gilbert Start Date: 8/25/2026 Assist with game-day media operations including statistics, photography, live streaming, and public address. Ideal for students with an interest in sports communication, broadcasting, and media production. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Assist with games statistics – C, T, CT Take pictures at games for UPIKEbears.com – T, P, C Public address announcing at select sports – C, P, TW Run cameras for live streams of select sports – T, P, CT Competencies/Skills: Career & Self Development (CSD), Communication (C), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Professionalism (P), Teamwork (TW), Technology (T) Preferred Skills: Computer knowledge (Word, Social Media & New Technology), basic athletics knowledge, attention to detail, public speaking, written & verbal communication, willingness to learn new things. Work Schedule: Saturday–Sunday: Varies depending on workload and home game schedules. Work hours can be flexible to accommodate student class schedules. Work Conditions: Heat, cold, noise, wetness, humidity, dust, light intensity, electrical currents. Physical Demands: Keyboarding, reaching/handling, stooping/kneeling, lifting up to 20 lbs., climbing. Number of Positions: 2–3 Pay Rate: $8.75/hour Location: Hoops Athletic Center To Apply: Complete required sections and upload your academic and practice schedule, along with your resume. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The