    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/472": {
      "title": "WS - Organic Chemistry Teaching Assistant - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Organic Chemistry Teaching Assistant - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. ORGANIC CHEMISTRY TEACHING ASSISTANT Division: CAS Department: Chemistry Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSFACASTCHEM Supervisor/Reports To: Kameyo Johnson Start Date: 8/25/2026 Support Organic Chemistry labs by preparing materials, guiding students, and upholding lab safety. Ideal for students with strong lab skills, attention to detail, and a passion for chemistry. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Maintain confidentiality, be punctual, communicate schedule changes in advance, and wear appropriate attire – P Assist with lab set-up, including making standard solutions and unknowns; operate lab instrumentation independently – TW, CT, T Assist students and answer questions during lab; support inclusivity in a diverse setting – C, CT, L, CTR Manage databases for the chemistry department – CT, T Modify or create handouts for chemistry classes – C, CT, T, P Type information, concepts, and formulas to assist students – C, CT, T, P Cleaning of glassware in the chemistry laboratories. – TW, P, CSD Maintain confidentiality, be punctual, communicate schedule changes in advance, and wear appropriate attire – P Assist with lab set-up, including making standard solutions and unknowns; operate lab instrumentation independently – TW, CT, T Assist students and answer questions during lab; Foster a collaborative environment that values individuals from varied perspectives – C, CT, L, CTR Create highly engaging PowerPoint slides, including embedded media and animation – T, CT, C Ensure all safety regulations are followed by students and self – P, L, CT Ensure the lab is clean and the equipment is returned and powered off after sessions – C, TW, L Provide clerical support, proofreading, photocopying, and filing; assist with projects as assigned – TW Prioritize responsibilities and meet deadlines successfully – P, L Effectively communicate your skills and availability in your application – CSD Perform other duties as determined by the supervisor – P, TW Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Preferred Skills: Word, Excel, PowerPoint, attention to detail, strong active listening abilities, public speaking, written & verbal communication, willingness to learn new things. Work Schedule: 9-12 hours a week Work Conditions: Toxic Agents, Machinery Physical Demands: Number of Positions: up to 3 Pay Rate: $10.50/hour Location: Armington 3rd floor. Rooms ARM 313 and ARM 322. To Apply: Complete required sections of application and upload resume. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/473": {
      "title": "WS - Biology Research Technician II - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Biology Research Technician II - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. Biology Research Technician II Division: CAS Department: Biology Experience: Intermediate Job Code: NA Supervisor of Student Employee(s): Byron Meade Requested Start Date: 08/24/2026 Students will assist in the management of various research projects within the natural sciences. These projects will typically be agriculturally focused, with a heavy emphasis on mushrooms, but could also include work in medicinal plant/fungal extracts. Students in this position will be given advanced research responsibilities, include data analyzing and preforming standardized experiments. This position is ideal for students interested in biological sciences and research experience. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Organize and maintain a clean and working research laboratory: C, TW, P Assist senior research personnel in prepping sterile substrates (agar, grain, etc…): C, TW, P, CSD, CT, L, T Assist with the design and implementation of novel agriculture research projects: C, TW, P, CSD, CT, CTR, L, T Inoculate, incubate, and harvest mushrooms and hydroponic vegetables: C, TW, P, L, T, CSD Oversee Biology Research Technician I employee’s maintenance on hydroponic and mushroom cultivation units: C, TW, T, CSD, L Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) In the following sections check all boxes that apply to your job. Computer Skills: Word, Excel, PowerPoint Other Skills: Attention to detail, Strong active listening abilities, Public speaking, Written & verbal communication, Willingness to learn new things Work Schedule: Hours vary depending on workload Work Conditions: Heat, Cold, Light Intensity, Humidity Physical Demands: Keyboarding, Reaching/Handling, Stooping/Kneeling, Crouching/Crawling, Pushing up to 50 lbs., Pulling up to 50 lbs., Lifting up to 50 lbs., Carrying up to 50 lbs. Number of Positions: 1 Pay Rate: 10.50/hour Location: Building: ARM, Room#: 110 Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/475": {
      "title": "WS - Biology Research Technician III- Senior Researcher - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Biology Research Technician III- Senior Researcher - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. Biology Research Technician III – Senior Researcher Division: CAS Department: Biology Experience: Advanced Job Code: NA Supervisor of Student Employee(s): Byron Meade Requested Start Date: 08/24/2026 Support faculty-led biological research in hydroponic agriculture, mycology, and molecular biology. Ideal for students from any academic background with an interest in lab work and scientific inquiry. This is a senior research position, which involves overseeing a small team of associate student researchers. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Assist with day-to-day research activities such as cleaning the lab, operating the autoclave, sterile benchtop work, and hydroponic maintenance – C, TW, P, CSD, CT, L, T Oversee other associate student researchers in their day to day tasks – C, TW, P, CSD, CT, L, T Maintain hydroponic plants and prepare roots for testing – C, T, P, CSD Assist with literature reviews for related topics – C, TW, L Prepare research documents and papers and help guide associate student researchers during the process – C, P, CSD, CTR, T, L Perform lab techniques such as PCR and DNA analysis – T, CSD, C, P Present findings in oral and/or written form – C, T, P, CTR, CT, L Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Computer Skills: Word, Excel, PowerPoint Other Skills: Attention to detail, Strong active listening abilities, Public speaking, Written & verbal communication, Willingness to learn new things Work Schedule: Hours vary depending on workload Work Conditions: Heat, Cold, Light Intensity, Wetness, Humidity Physical Demands: Keyboarding, Reaching/Handling, Stooping/Kneeling Crouching/Crawling, Pushing up to 50 lbs., Pulling up to 50 lbs., Lifting up to 50 lbs., Number of Positions: 1 Pay Rate: $12.50/hr Location: Building: ARM, Room#: 110 Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
