    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/480": {
      "title": "WS - Business Affairs Office Assistant - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Business Affairs Office Assistant - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. BUSINESS AFFAIRS OFFICE ASSISTANT Division: Support Services Department: Finance & Business Affairs Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSBUSOFFAST Supervisor/Reports To: Brandi Gollihue Start Date: 8/24/2026 Provide clerical support in the Business Affairs Office by filing, organizing, scanning, and delivering documents. Ideal for students with attention to detail, organizational skills, and an interest in administrative work. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Filing and organizing documents in both digital and paper formats – C, P, T Scanning documents and saving them to appropriate locations – C, T, P Delivering documents and materials across campus – TW, C, P Preparing and sorting paperwork for processing – C, CT, P Maintaining confidentiality and following office procedures – P, C, TW Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Preferred Skills: Word, Excel, attention to detail, strong active listening abilities, willingness to learn new things. Work Schedule: Monday–Friday, 10 hours per week (flexible). Work Conditions: Normal office environment. Physical Demands: Keyboarding, reaching, stooping, lifting/carrying up to 25 lbs. Number of Positions: 1 Pay Rate: $8.75/hour Location: Business Affairs Office, Administration Building To Apply: Complete application and upload resume. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. ."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/481": {
      "title": "WS - Office Assistant for Dean's Office - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Office Assistant for Dean's Office - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. OFFICE ASSISTANT FOR DEAN'S OFFICE Division: CAS Department: Dean's Office Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSCASOFFASTDN Supervisor/Reports To: Donna Hunt Start Date: 8/24/2026 Support the Dean’s Office by maintaining supplies, providing clerical assistance, and assisting with events. Ideal for students who are detail-oriented, self-motivated, and comfortable working in a professional environment. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Organize and maintain supplies in classrooms and collaboration hub – CT, P Assist with and contribute to events hosted by professional staff – C, TW, P Work independently and efficiently; use available resources to direct guests – CT, P Make campus deliveries and provide clerical support including proofreading, photocopying, and filing – TW, P Work on additional projects as assigned – TW Use MS Word, Excel, multi-line phone system, and compile data using software programs – T Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Preferred Skills: Word; written & verbal communication, customer-focused, willingness to learn new things. Work Schedule: 5–10 hours per week, Monday–Friday between 8am–5pm, varies depending on availability. Work Conditions: Normal office environment. Physical Demands: Keyboarding, reaching/handling, stooping/kneeling. Number of Positions: 1 Pay Rate: $8.75/hour Location: Armington 219 To Apply: Complete required sections of application and upload resume. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/482": {
      "title": "WS - Softball Operations Assistant - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Softball Operations Assistant - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. Softball Operations Assistant Division: Athletics Department: Softball Experience: Entry-level Job Code: TBD Supervisor of Student Employee(s): April Charles Requested Start Date: August 24, 2026 Assist in the everyday operations of a college softball program. Main duties include officiating junior varsity games, game day field prep and operations, and analyzing data associated with opponents and individual practice sessions. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Officiate Junior Varsity games. Game day field preparations: Line the field, prepare field for games, set up scoreboard, sound system, etc Practice preparation: get out bases, equipment, set up stations Data collection during individual sessions. Collect data to assist in individual development (i.e. track amount of strikes thrown for pitchers, track locations and pitches hit for hitters) Assist in analyzing films of opponents. Assist in social media content Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Computer Skills: Word, Excel, Canva, Social Media & New Technology Other Skills: Attention to detail, Strong active listening abilities, Willingness to learn new things Work Schedule: Hours vary depending on workload Work Conditions: Heat, Cold, Dust, Light Intensity, Humidity Physical Demands: Keyboarding, Stooping/Kneeling Number of Positions: 4 Pay Rate: $8.75/hour Location: Paul Butcher Field/Gym/Hoops/Cages Additional Comments: Knowledge of softball rules is a must. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/483": {
      "title": "WS - Assistant to CAS Administrative & Engagement Coordinator - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Assistant to CAS Administrative & Engagement Coordinator - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. Assistant to CAS Administrative & Engagement Coordinator Division: CAS Department: Dean’s Office Experience: Entry-level Job Code: TBD Supervisor/Reports To: Hannah Justice Requested Start Date: 8/24/2026 The candidate’s main role is to assist the College of Arts & Sciences with duties pertaining to all CAS event organizations upon request. The College of Arts & Sciences is made up of three departments (Humanities, Math & Science, and Social Sciences) with many programs that fall under these departments; all events that require assistance (upon request from CAS faculty) will be facilitated by CAS Administrative & Engagement Coordinator and assistant(s). Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Putting together smaller packets/materials for event purposes (educational worksheets provided by faculty, UPIKE swag bags/items for tables, etc.) - C, TW, P Moving equipment to and from event (smaller scale) – must be able to accommodate and communicate all academic conflicts with events in a timely fashion - C, TW, P, CT Create flyers (as assigned) for events and receive feedback for edits by CAS Engagement & Administrative Coordinator - C, TW, P, CT, T Hanging up flyers and posters on appropriate bulletin boards on campus in a timely manner prior to event - C, TW, P Work as greeters & man tables at larger scale events where CAS Engagement & Administrative Coordinator is present and occupied with other event related tasks - C, TW, P, L, CTR Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Computer Skills: Word, Excel, Canva, Social Media & New Technology Other Skills: Attention to detail, Strong active listening abilities, Public speaking, Written & verbal communication, Customer focused, Willingness to learn new things Work Schedule: M-F 12 to 5; Hours vary depending on workload *Some events take place outside of regular school & work hours Physical Demands: Reaching/Handling, Stooping/Kneeling, Lifting up to 30lbs., Carrying up to 15lbs. Number of Positions: 1-3 Pay Rate: $ 8.75/hour Location: Building: Record Memorial Building, Room#: 401 Additional Comments: Complete required sections of application and upload resume. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/484": {
      "title": "WS - Writing Center Peer Consultant",
      "description": "WS - Writing Center Peer Consultant. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. WRITING CENTER PEER CONSULTANT Division: CAS Department: Writing Center Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSWRTCTRPC Supervisor/Reports To: Beth Topping Start Date: 8/24/2026 Provide peer support in writing and composing for academic, campus work, and application needs. Ideal for students with strong writing, communication, and interpersonal skills. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Provide writing and composing support for academic, campus work, and application purposes – C, TW, P, CSD, CT Conduct campus and classroom presentations to raise awareness of the Center – L, P, C Conduct workshops on professional, graduate, and internship applications; research documentation; digital tools; and others as assigned – L, TW, P, C Maintain accurate records of each consultation through WCOnline – P, T Assist in developing student and faculty resources; training materials; online content; and others as needed – TW, P, CSD, CT Attend meetings as required – P Develop and pitch ideas to prepare Writing Center for August 2025 launch – CSD, CT, L Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Preferred Skills: Word, PowerPoint, WCOnline, attention to detail, strong active listening abilities, public speaking, customer service, willingness to learn new things, written and verbal communication skills. Work Schedule: Available between Monday–Thursday, 10 AM – 3 PM. No more than 10 hrs per week. Work Conditions: May encounter heat or cold, noise, or humidity. Physical Demands: Keyboarding, reaching, stooping, lifting/carrying up to 15 lbs. Number of Positions: 3–5 Pay Rate: $9.75/hour Location: Armington Learning Center, 4th floor, Room #450 To Apply: Upload application, resume, cover letter, and class schedule. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If you meet the qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/485": {
      "title": "WS - Elkhorn City Elementary School Tutor - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Elkhorn City Elementary School Tutor - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. ELKHORN CITY ELEMENTARY TUTOR Division: Support Services Department: Admissions Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSECELEMTUTOR Supervisor/Reports To: Sonia Smith; Amber Cantrell (Principal) Start Date: 8/25/2026 Provide one-on-one and small group tutoring in reading and math for elementary students. Ideal for students who are patient, communicative, and eager to support early learners with guided training. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Provide one-on-one reading assistance to identified students – C, P Provide small group reading and/or math assistance to identified students – C, CT, P Train with on-site supervisor for effective tutoring practices – C, CT, P Engage with students to evaluate progress – C, P Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Preferred Skills: Attention to detail, active listening, public speaking, written & verbal communication, willingness to learn. Work Schedule: Monday–Friday based on school needs and student class schedule. No weekend hours. Work Conditions: Normal school environment; may include noise. Physical Demands: Keyboarding, stooping/kneeling. Additional Notes: Tutors must maintain confidentiality. Paid training provided. Duties include assisting elementary students with reading and/or math, helping with homework, and reinforcing reading skills and comprehension. A free background check is required before beginning. Number of Positions: 2–4 Pay Rate: $10.50/hour Location: Elkhorn City Elementary School, 180 Cougar Drive, Elkhorn City, KY 45122. Let us know if you have transportation when applying. To Apply: Complete required sections and upload your academic and practice schedule, along with your resume. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/486": {
      "title": "WS - Campus Employment Office Assistant - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Campus Employment Office Assistant - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. Campus Employment Office Assistant Division: Human Resources Department: Campus Employment Experience: Entry-level Job Code: TBD Supervisor/Reports To: Sonia Smith Start Date: 8/25/2026 The Student Office Worker provides administrative and clerical support to the Campus Employment and HR team. This role helps maintain accurate employee records, assists with onboarding, and ensures smooth daily office operations through communication and attention to detail. The position contributes to recruitment visibility and supports special projects as needed. Answer phones and direct calls to appropriate staff in a professional manner – C, P Greet visitors and provide a welcoming, professional first impression of the department – C, P Organize and maintain employee files (physical and digital) while protecting confidential information – CT, P Copy, scan, and fax documents to support HR administrative workflows – T, P Schedule appointments and coordinate meetings, assisting staff with calendar management – T, TW Perform accurate data entry and maintain up-to-date records in HR systems – T, CT Assist with onboarding by preparing new hire paperwork and materials – P, CSD Prepare memos, forms, and other correspondence related to campus employment policies and procedures – C, T Support campus employment projects, including research and basic data analysis – CT, T, CSD Help with marketing and recruitment efforts to increase visibility of campus employment opportunities – C, TW, CTR Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self-Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Education Requirements: Must be a current UPIKE student in good standing. Preferred Skills: Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, Outlook); strong communication and interpersonal skills; attention to detail; ability to handle confidential information; customer service orientation; willingness to learn new systems. Work Schedule: Up to 10 hours per week; schedule varies depending on office needs and student availability. Work Conditions: Typical office environment; may include occasional interruptions or varied lighting/noise levels. Physical Demands: Keyboarding; reaching/handling; occasional lifting up to 10 lbs. Number of Positions: 2 Pay Rate: $8.75/hour Location: Administrative building ground floor, Campus Employment office To Apply: Submit application and resume through the UPIKE campus employment system. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/487": {
      "title": "WS - Campus Employment Marketing/Social Media/Content Creator - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Campus Employment Marketing/Social Media/Content Creator - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. CAMPUS EMPLOYMENT MARKETING/SOCIAL MEDIA/CONTENT CREATOR Division: Support Services Department: Campus Employment Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSSTDEMPAST Supervisor/Reports To: Sonia Smith Start Date: 8/25/2026 Assist in creating, collecting, and analyzing marketing data while developing content for campus employment initiatives. Ideal for students with an interest in marketing, data analysis, and creative content production. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Develop and update marketing materials for campus employment programs – C, TW, P, CT, T Create digital content including graphics, videos, and written materials – C, T, P, CSD Manage social media posts and updates related to campus employment – C, T Maintain records and compile reports for supervisor – C, P, CT Collaborate with other departments and student workers to promote events and marketing initiatives – TW, L, C, P Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Preferred Skills: Word, Excel, Social Media & New Technology, attention to detail, strong active listening abilities, willingness to learn new things. Work Schedule: Monday–Friday, 10 hours per week; hours flexible around student schedule. Work Conditions: Normal office environment. Physical Demands: Keyboarding, reaching, stooping, lifting up to 20 lbs. Number of Positions: 1 Pay Rate: $9.75/hour Location: Campus Employment Office / HPE 301 To Apply: Complete application and upload resume. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/489": {
      "title": "WS - Title IX Program Assistant",
      "description": "WS - Title IX Program Assistant. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. Title IX Program Assistant Division: President’s Office Department: Title IX Office Experience: Entry level Job Code: GL Code: [ Supervisor of Student Employee(s): Beth Kingery FWS, IWS, or Grant Funded: ☐ FWS, ☐ IWS, ☐ Grant Funded Avg. Hours/Week: ☐ 1-5, ☒ 6-10, ☐ 11-15, ☐ 16-20 Requested Start Date: 08/-3126 Term of Position: ☐ Summer, ☒ Fall, ☒ Spring The Title IX Program Assistant helps support UPIKE's Title IX office by assisting with prevention and awareness efforts across campus. This role includes helping with educational events, creating outreach materials, updating resources, and providing general administrative support. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Assist with planning and promoting Title IX awareness events and prevention programs throughout the academic year. C, TW, P, CTR Create flyers, social media content, presentations, and other educational materials to increase campus awareness of Title IX resources. C, T, CT, CTR Help maintain and update the Title IX website, brochures, and campus resource information. C, P, T Assist with scheduling trainings, workshops, and outreach activities for students, faculty, and staff. C, TW, P Track participation in trainings and educational programs and help organize attendance records. P, T, CT Provide general administrative support, including organizing files, preparing materials, and assisting with special projects P, TW, CSD Competencies/Skills: Communication ©, Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Qualifications: Organized and dependable Comfortable with student engagement and outreach Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information appropriately In the following sections check all boxes that apply to your job. Computer Skills: ☒ Word, ☒ Excel, ☒ PowerPoint, ☒ Canva, ☒ Social Media & New Technology, ☐ Other: _________________________ Other Skills: ☐ Attention to detail, ☐ Strong active listening abilities, ☐ Public speaking, ☒ Written & verbal communication, ☐ Customer focused, ☒ Willingness to learn new things Work Schedule: ☐ Su ___ to ___; ☐ M ___ to ___; ☐ T ___ to ___; ☐ W ___ to ___; ☐ R ___ to ___; ☐ F ___ to ___; ☐ Sa ___ to ___; ☒ Hours vary depending on workload (Check days that apply, insert hours if set, otherwise, check “Hours vary depending on workload”.) Work Conditions: ☐ Heat, ☐ Cold, ☐ Odors/Smoke, ☐ Toxic Agents, ☐ Dust, ☐ Machinery, ☐ Light Intensity, ☐ Noise, ☐ Vibrations, ☐ Wetness, ☐ Humidity, ☐ Electrical Currents, ☐ Other: _________________________ Physical Demands: ☒ Keyboarding, ☐ Reaching/Handling, ☐ Stooping/Kneeling, ☐ Crouching/Crawling, ☐ Pushing up to ___ lbs., ☐ Pulling up to ___ lbs., ☐ Lifting up to ___ lbs., ☐ Carrying up to ___ lbs., ☐ Climbing, ☐ Balancing, ☐ Other: _________________________ Number of Positions: 1 Pay Rate: $8.75/hr Location: Building: 119 Caroline Avenue, Pikeville, KY Additional Comments: Currently enrolled UPIKE student who is dependable, professional, organized, and willing to learn. Strong communication skills and an interest in campus education, student support, communications, or event planning are helpful. Training will be provided. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/490": {
      "title": "WS - Health Professions Admissions Assistant - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Health Professions Admissions Assistant - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. HEALTH PROFESSIONS ADMISSIONS ASSISTANT Division: Support Services Department: Admissions Experience: Entry Level Job Code: TBD Supervisor/Reports To: Jennifer Lockhart Provide front-line administrative support for Health Professions Admissions by greeting visitors, answering inquiries, and assisting with application processing. This role helps maintain organized records, supports admissions events, and delivers a welcoming experience for prospective students and families. Serve as first point of contact at the front desk: answer calls, greet visitors, route inquiries, and schedule appointments – C, P, CT Process and track application materials: data entry, scanning/filing, and maintaining confidential records – T, P, CT Support admissions events and interview days: prepare materials, manage check-in, and assist guests – TW, C, P Monitor shared email/inboxes; provide accurate information using scripts/templates and escalate complex cases – C, CT, P Maintain spreadsheets/reports for prospects and applicants; update contact lists and mailing databases – T, CT, P Contribute to special projects (e.g., outreach lists, mailings, deliveries) and other duties as assigned – TW, P Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self-Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Education Requirements: Must be a current UPIKE student in good standing. Preferred Skills: Word; Excel; PowerPoint; attention to detail; strong active listening; written & verbal communication; willingness to learn. Work Schedule: M–F, varies depending on workload; up to 20 hours/week; no Sunday/Saturday hours. Work Conditions: Typical office environment. Physical Demands: Keyboarding; reaching/handling; occasional lifting/carrying up to 20 lbs. Pay Rate: $9.75/hour Location: Admissions Office – HPE 6th Floor Number of Positions: 1 To Apply: Submit application and resume through the UPIKE campus employment system. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/496": {
      "title": "WS - IT and AV Events Support Tech Level I",
      "description": "WS - IT and AV Events Support Tech Level I. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. IT AV EVENTS & SUPPORT TECHNICIAN LEVEL I Division: Support Services Department: Information Technology Services Experience: Advanced Job Code: TBD Supervisor/Reports To: Charlie Cable Start Date: 9/02/2026 Provide expert-level AV and IT support for both live events and classroom technology. Serve as a lead technician for high-profile, technically complex events and support day-to-day classroom technology operations. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Support the coordination and execution of campus events by assisting with IT and A/V setup and troubleshooting. This role is ideal for students interested in event operations, technology, and hands-on experience in live production and customer service. You will work closely with IT staff and event organizers to ensure events run smoothly and professionally. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Assist with the setup, operation, and teardown of A/V and IT equipment for campus events – C, TW, P, T Monitor and support A/V equipment during live events (e.g., microphones, projectors, sound systems, A/V accessories) – C, TW, P, T Provide on-site assistance during events, including basic troubleshooting and tech support – C, TW, CT, P, T Communicate with event staff, faculty, and IT supervisors to ensure needs are met regarding issues and scheduling – C, TW, P Assist with inventory management, equipment maintenance, and proper storage – C, P, T Uphold safety standards and follow proper procedures for equipment handling – P, T Represent the university professionally while engaging with event guests and participants – P, C, TW Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) In the following sections check all boxes that apply to your job. Computer Skills: ☒ Word, ☒ Excel, ☒ PowerPoint, ☐ Canva, ☒ Social Media & New Technology, ☐ Other: _________________________ Other Skills: ☒ Attention to detail, ☒ Strong active listening abilities, ☐ Public speaking, ☒ Written & verbal communication, ☒ Customer focused, ☒ Willingness to learn new things Work Schedule: ☐ Su ___ to ___; ☐ M ___ to ___; ☐ T ___ to ___; ☐ W ___ to ___; ☐ R ___ to ___; ☐ F ___ to ___; ☐ Sa ___ to ___; ☒ Hours vary depending on workload (Check days that apply, insert hours if set, otherwise, check “Hours vary depending on workload”.) Work Conditions: ☒ Heat, ☒ Cold, ☐ Odors/Smoke, ☐ Toxic Agents, ☐ Dust, ☐ Machinery, ☒ Light Intensity, ☒ Noise, ☒ Vibrations, ☒ Wetness, ☒ Humidity, ☐ Electrical Currents, ☐ Other: _________________________ Physical Demands: ☐ Keyboarding, ☒ Reaching/Handling, ☒ Stooping/Kneeling, ☒ Crouching/Crawling, ☒ Pushing up to _50_ lbs., ☒ Pulling up to _50_ lbs., ☒ Lifting up to _50_ lbs., ☒ Carrying up to _50_ lbs., ☒ Climbing, ☐ Balancing, ☐ Other: _________________________ Number of Positions: 4 Pay Rate: 9.75 Location: Armington 017 Additional Comments: Add additional comments for job applicants here. [DO NOT CHANGE ANYTHING BELOW THIS POINT] Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/497": {
      "title": "WS - IT and AV Events Support Tech Level 2",
      "description": "WS - IT and AV Events Support Tech Level 2. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. IT AV EVENTS & SUPPORT TECHNICIAN LEVEL 2 Division: Support Services Department: Information Technology Services Experience: Advanced Job Code: TBD Supervisor/Reports To: Charlie Cable Start Date: 9/02/2026 Support the planning and execution of campus events by assisting with advanced A/V and IT operations. This position is ideal for students with prior experience in event support or A/V technology who are looking to expand their leadership and troubleshooting skills. In addition to set-up and monitoring, Level 2 assistants will help train new student staff, troubleshoot real-time issues, and serve as primary contacts for on-site event tech support when needed. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Lead or assist with setup and teardown of complex A/V and IT systems for campus events – C, TW, P, T, L Serve as on-site technical support for events, handling troubleshooting and escalated issues – CT, T, C, P Provide guidance, mentorship, and informal training to Level 1 student staff – L, TW, C, P Coordinate closely with event organizers and university staff to confirm A/V requirements – C, P, TW, CT Assist in testing and configuring advanced A/V systems, including A/V over IP setups and hybrid event platforms – T, CT, P Maintain equipment inventory and assist with routine maintenance and updates – T, P Act as a liaison between the IT department and event coordinators to ensure high-quality service – C, P, CTR Support ongoing efforts to improve processes and event tech procedures – CT, L, CSD Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) In the following sections check all boxes that apply to your job. Computer Skills: ☒ Word, ☒ Excel, ☒ PowerPoint, ☐ Canva, ☒ Social Media & New Technology, ☐ Other: _________________________ Other Skills: ☒ Attention to detail, ☒ Strong active listening abilities, ☐ Public speaking, ☒ Written & verbal communication, ☒ Customer focused, ☒ Willingness to learn new things Work Schedule: ☐ Su ___ to ___; ☐ M ___ to ___; ☐ T ___ to ___; ☐ W ___ to ___; ☐ R ___ to ___; ☐ F ___ to ___; ☐ Sa ___ to ___; ☒ Hours vary depending on workload (Check days that apply, insert hours if set, otherwise, check “Hours vary depending on workload”.) Work Conditions: ☒ Heat, ☒ Cold, ☐ Odors/Smoke, ☐ Toxic Agents, ☐ Dust, ☐ Machinery, ☒ Light Intensity, ☒ Noise, ☒ Vibrations, ☒ Wetness, ☒ Humidity, ☐ Electrical Currents, ☐ Other: _________________________ Physical Demands: ☐ Keyboarding, ☒ Reaching/Handling, ☒ Stooping/Kneeling, ☒ Crouching/Crawling, ☒ Pushing up to _50_ lbs., ☒ Pulling up to _50_ lbs., ☒ Lifting up to _50_ lbs., ☒ Carrying up to _50_ lbs., ☒ Climbing, ☐ Balancing, ☐ Other: _________________________ Number of Positions: 1 Pay Rate: 10.50 Location: Armington 017 Additional Comments: Add additional comments for job applicants here. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
