    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/518": {
      "title": "WS - Presidential Fellows - IWS",
      "description": "WS - Presidential Fellows - IWS. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. This position is reserved exclusively for Presidential Fellows. If you are not a Presidential Fellow, please do not apply. Presidential Fellows – Experiential Learning & Leadership Placement Presidential Fellows participate in meaningful, individualized experiences designed to complement their academic interests, career goals, and areas they wish to explore. Placements vary by student and may include research, communications, leadership, project development, community engagement, administrative initiatives, or other professional experiences. Each Fellow is matched with a faculty or staff mentor and provided opportunities to develop transferable skills, build professional relationships, take on increasing responsibility, and gain exposure to people and experiences that support their future academic and career goals. Presidential Fellows are expected to actively participate in their placement, communicate professionally with their mentor, reflect on what they are learning, and contribute meaningfully to the work of the department or program. Placements may evolve as the Fellow develops new skills and interests. The goal is not simply to complete assigned tasks, but to provide an intentional learning experience that helps Fellows connect their academic studies, practical experience, leadership development, and future aspirations. #LI-DNI"
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/519": {
      "title": "WS - MarCom Student Assistant Level II - FWS",
      "description": "WS - MarCom Student Assistant Level II - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. MARCOM STUDENT ASSISTANT LEVEL II Division: Support Services Department: Marketing & Communications (MarCom) Experience: Intermediate Job Code: FWSPRSTDAST Supervisor/Reports To: Kate Hensley Start Date: 8/24/2026 Support the Marketing & Communications department with tasks related to photography, videography, social media content creation, and office duties. Ideal for creative students interested in digital media, storytelling, and communications. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Help train and manage level 1 work studies L Greet and answer guests’ questions that come to the office when working at the front desk. P, C Conceptualize content for the university’s social media and work with level 1 work studies to create it. L, C,T,EI, CSD Operate and manage the university printer. Prioritize print jobs based on importance. Keep track of paper inventory T, CSD Complete finishing work on university publications (binding, cutting, sorting, etc.). T Provide administrative assistance, including picking up packages, organizing spaces, internet research or data entry. This could include using programs like Microsoft Word, Excel, etc. TW Help staff members with various projects/tasks. TW, CSD Maintain bulletin boards on campus by decorating and posting flyers. C Work with the MarComm team on-campus events TW Maintain confidentiality, be punctual, and communicate changes in the work schedule in advance, Appropriate attire as discussed for work environment. P Other tasks, as needed or assigned. Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Preferred Skills: Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Social Media & New Technology, Adobe Creative Cloud, strong active listening abilities, attention to detail, written & verbal communication, willingness to learn new things. Work Schedule: Monday–Friday, flexible around class schedule, up to 10-20 hours per week. Work Conditions: Office and event settings; may include indoor and outdoor environments. May be subject to noise, dust and machinery in the printer room. Physical Demands: Keyboarding, reaching/handling, stooping/kneeling, pushing up to 20 lbs., pulling up to 20 lbs., lifting up to 20 lbs., carrying up to 20 lbs. Number of Positions: 1 Pay Rate: $ 9.75/hour Location: Administration Building, 1st Floor, MarComm Suite and Wickham Printing Room To Apply: Complete required sections of application and upload resume. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If you meet the qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
