    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/525": {
      "title": "WS - Research Assistant Prater - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Research Assistant Prater - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. RESEARCH ASSISTANT (Prater) Division: CAS Department: Biology Experience: Intermediate‑level Job Code: NA Supervisor of Student Employee(s): Peyton Prater Requested Start Date: 8/24/2026 Support faculty‑led field research by assisting with outdoor data collection, equipment setup, and accurate record‑keeping. This role contributes to ecological and environmental projects conducted on and off campus and develops hands‑on skills in safe, professional fieldwork and basic data management. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Conduct outdoor field surveys to collect biological, ecological, or environmental data – CT, C, P, TW Record, organize, and maintain accurate field notes and data sheets using digital or written formats – CT, T, P Assist with setup, calibration, and use of field research equipment (e.g., GPS units, sampling nets, environmental sensors) – T, P, CSD Work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and peers to complete field projects and research goals – TW, L, C Ensure safety protocols are followed in outdoor environments (use of protective gear, awareness of hazards) – P, CT, L Contribute to data entry, preliminary analysis, and preparation of research reports or presentations – T, C, CT Engage respectfully with local communities, landowners, and partners during off‑campus fieldwork – C, CTR, P Demonstrate initiative by learning new field methods, research tools, and environmental monitoring techniques – CSD, T, CT Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Computer Skills: GIS Software Other Skills: Attention to detail, , Written & verbal communication, Customer focused, Willingness to learn new things Work Schedule: Hours vary depending on workload Work Conditions: Heat, Cold, Odors/Smoke, Light Intensity, Wetness, Humidity Physical Demands: Reaching/Handling, Crouching/Crawling, Pushing up to 50 lbs., Climbing, Balancing, Number of Positions: 2 Hours needed per week: 15 per student Pay Rate: $10.50/hour Location: Off campus – The Breaks Interstate Park (with some on‑campus work possible) Additional Comments: Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/526": {
      "title": "WS - Jubilee Center Assistant for Bear Minimum Thrift - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Jubilee Center Assistant for Bear Minimum Thrift - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. Jubilee Center Assistant for Bear Minimum Thrift Division: Support Services Department: Wellbeing/Health Experience: Entry-level Job Code: NA Supervisor of Student Employee(s): Robert Musick Requested Start Date: 8/24/2026 The Bear Minimum Campus Thrift Store located in the Jubilee Center is looking for assistants. This is a Federal Work-Study position that supports the daily operations of the campus thrift store while promoting affordability, sustainability, and student engagement. The student employee assists with customer service, inventory management, merchandising, and store operations, helping create an organized, welcoming shopping experience for the campus community. Responsibilities and Career Competencies Greet customers and provide friendly, professional service to students, faculty, staff, and visitors. (C, P, CTR) Receive, sort, inspect, and organize donated merchandise according to store guidelines. (P, CT, TW) Price, label, display, and restock merchandise while maintaining organized sales areas. (P, CT, CSD) Operate the point-of-sale system and accurately process transactions. (P, T, CT) Assist with inventory, donation records, and basic data entry. (T, P, CT) Promote Bear Minimum through events, social media, and campus outreach. (C, T, L, CTR) Support sales, donation drives, special events, and sustainability initiatives. (TW, L, CTR) Maintain a clean, safe, and welcoming store environment. (P, TW) Collaborate with supervisors, volunteers, and student employees while demonstrating dependability and responsible stewardship. (TW, P, CSD, CTR) Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) In the following sections check all boxes that apply to your job. Computer Skills: