    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/536": {
      "title": "WS - Contact Lens Assistant III - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Contact Lens Assistant III - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. CONTACT LENS ASSISTANT LEVEL III Division: KYCO Department: Student Affairs Experience: Advanced Job Code: FWSKYCOCLASIII Supervisor/Reports To: Dominique Fulk Start Date: 8/25/2026 The Contact Lens Assistant Level III supports clinical faculty and students in the contact lens labs and maintains supplies. This position plays an essential role in lab setup, inventory, and assisting in student and patient-related preparation. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Maintain and stock contact lens supplies for the contact lens lab – P, T Assist with organization and cleanliness of the contact lens rooms – P, CSD Maintain cleanliness of clinical equipment, including trial lenses and solutions – P, T Assist in the preparation and restocking of supplies for student labs – TW, P Provide support during clinical lab sessions when students need materials or troubleshooting help – TW, C, T Collaborate with supervisors to maintain accurate inventory lists – CT, T, P May assist with tracking and organizing patient contact lens orders under supervision – C, T, P Complete assigned administrative or clerical duties related to lab upkeep – P, T Communicate with faculty or staff regarding needs, issues, or requests in the lab – C, TW Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self-Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Education Requirements: Must be a current UPIKE student in good standing. Preferred Skills: Attention to detail, time management, ability to follow procedures, communication skills, organization. Work Schedule: Up to 10 hours per week during operational hours of the contact lens lab. Work Conditions: Clinical lab and office environment. Physical Demands: Standing, lifting supplies, reaching, and occasional movement between lab spaces. Number of Positions: 1 Pay Rate: 12.50/hr Location: KYCO Contact Lens Lab To Apply: Submit application and resume through the UPIKE campus employment system. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/537": {
      "title": "WS - Contact Lens Assistant II- FWS",
      "description": "WS - Contact Lens Assistant II- FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. CONTACT LENS ASSISTANT LEVEL II Division: KYCO Department: Student Affairs Experience: Advanced Job Code: FWSKYCOCLASII Supervisor/Reports To: Renee Reeder Start Date: 8/25/2026 The Contact Lens Assistant Level III supports clinical faculty and students in the contact lens labs and maintains supplies. This position plays an essential role in lab setup, inventory, and assisting in student and patient-related preparation. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Maintain and stock contact lens supplies for the contact lens lab – P, T Assist with organization and cleanliness of the contact lens rooms – P, CSD Maintain cleanliness of clinical equipment, including trial lenses and solutions – P, T Assist in the preparation and restocking of supplies for student labs – TW, P Provide support during clinical lab sessions when students need materials or troubleshooting help – TW, C, T Collaborate with supervisors to maintain accurate inventory lists – CT, T, P May assist with tracking and organizing patient contact lens orders under supervision – C, T, P Complete assigned administrative or clerical duties related to lab upkeep – P, T Communicate with faculty or staff regarding needs, issues, or requests in the lab – C, TW Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self-Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Education Requirements: Must be a current UPIKE student in good standing. Preferred Skills: Attention to detail, time management, ability to follow procedures, communication skills, organization. Work Schedule: Up to 10 hours per week during operational hours of the contact lens lab. Work Conditions: Clinical lab and office environment. Physical Demands: Standing, lifting supplies, reaching, and occasional movement between lab spaces. Number of Positions: 1 Pay Rate:10.50/hr Location: KYCO Contact Lens Lab To Apply: Submit application and resume through the UPIKE campus employment system. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/538": {
      "title": "WS - Contact Lens Assistant - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Contact Lens Assistant - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. CONTACT LENS ASSISTANT Division: KYCO Department: Academic Affairs Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSKYCOCLASI Supervisor/Reports To: Renee Reeder Start Date: 8/25/2026 Assist with maintaining contact lens inventory, processing student data, preparing supply kits, and supporting lab operations. Ideal for students interested in optometry or pre-optometry fields. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Inventory supplies and create list for restock – CSD Inventory contact lens fitting sets, scan for reorder, place orders as needed for lab – CSD Maintain google document of student data and assist with processing for CL orders for the lab – CSD, T, CT Create and maintain supply kits for use in lab – CSD, T Check in lenses and label them – T, CSD Keep track of lenses and supplies ordered – P, T, C Assist with ancillary testing as needed – C, P, CSD, CTR Clean, disinfect, inspect, verify and maintain contact lenses – CSD, T, CT Sort and assign students to lanes for workshops and labs using excel or google sheets – T, CSD, CT Interact with workshop/vendor organizer in preparation for special events – P, T, C, L Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Preferred Skills: Word, Excel, Google sign-ups and sheets, attention to detail, willingness to learn new things. Work Schedule: Wednesday: 9:00am - 12:00pm. Flexible to accommodate student schedule. Priority during open hours and special events. Work Conditions: Normal office environment. Physical Demands: Keyboarding, pulling up to 30 lbs, lifting and carrying up to 10 lbs. Number of Positions: 2 Pay Rate: $9.75/hour Location: HPE building 5th floor, KYCO office suite To Apply: Complete required sections and upload your academic schedule (and practice schedule) along with your resume. Application Notes: Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/539": {
      "title": "WS - Chemistry Teaching Assistant (Hess)",
      "description": "WS - Chemistry Teaching Assistant (Hess). Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. Chemistry Teaching Assistant Hess Division: CAS Department: Chemistry Experience: advanced Job Code: FWSCASCHEMTA Supervisor/Reports To: Tom Hess Start Date: 8/25/2026 Support General Chemistry and Quantitative Analysis labs by preparing materials, guiding students, and upholding lab safety. Ideal for students with strong lab skills, attention to detail, and a passion for chemistry. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Maintain confidentiality, be punctual, communicate schedule changes in advance, and wear appropriate attire – P Assist with lab set-up, including making standard solutions and unknowns; operate lab instrumentation independently – TW, CT, T Arrive 15 minutes before lab to ensure setup is complete before students arrive – P Assist students and answer questions during lab; Foster a collaborative environment that values individuals from varied perspectives – C, CT, L, CTR Ensure all safety regulations are followed by students and self – P, L, CT Ensure lab is clean and equipment is returned and powered off after sessions – C, TW, L Provide clerical support, proofreading, photocopying, and filing; assist with projects as assigned – TW Grade lab reports while maintaining confidentiality – C, P, CT Prioritize responsibilities and meet deadlines successfully – P, L Effectively communicate your skills and availability in your application – CSD Perform other duties as determined by the supervisor – P, TW Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Required Skills: Must have completed General Chemistry I and II and associated labs. Preferred Skills: Word, Excel, PowerPoint, attention to detail, strong active listening abilities, public speaking, written & verbal communication, willingness to learn new things. Student has completed at least organic chemistry and/or quantitative analysis. Work Schedule: 10 hours a week Work Conditions: Toxic Agents, Machinery Physical Demands: Number of Positions: 1 - 3 Pay Rate: $10.50/hour Location: Armington 3rd floor. Rooms ARM 303, ARM 312, and ARM 314 and associated stock rooms (ARM 312s, ARM 313s, and ARM 314s). To Apply: Complete required sections of application and upload resume. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/540": {
      "title": "Community Education - Dance Teaching Assistant",
      "description": "Community Education - Dance Teaching Assistant. Department: Community Ed Dance Program. Part-Time. The University of Pikeville is seeking an energetic and dependable Assistant Instructor to support the School of Dance program. This position works alongside lead instructors to provide a positive, structured, and encouraging studio environment for students across a variety of age groups and skill levels. The Assistant Instructor will help with classroom management, technique demonstrations, student engagement, rehearsals, and general studio operations. A foundational background in ballet is required. Additional training in jazz, hip-hop, lyrical, and/or tap is preferred. Responsibilities: Assist lead instructors with warm-ups, technical exercises, choreography, and other classroom activities. Support instruction in ballet, jazz, hip-hop, lyrical, tap, and other dance styles based on experience and program needs. Demonstrate dance techniques and movements accurately and appropriately for students. Provide individual assistance and support to students as needed. Help maintain student focus, classroom organization, and a safe studio environment. Assist with classroom transitions, attendance, and preparation of studio spaces. Help coordinate costumes, props, and other materials used for classes and performances. Assist with rehearsals, recitals, performances, and other School of Dance activities. Encourage students and help create a welcoming and positive learning environment. Perform other duties as assigned. Education and Experience: Formal dance training with foundational skills and technique in at least two dance genres, including ballet, jazz, hip-hop, lyrical, and/or tap. Foundational training in ballet is required. Previous experience working with children or youth is preferred. Previous teaching, assistant teaching, or dance studio experience is preferred but not required. Skills and Abilities: Ability to accurately demonstrate dance movements and techniques. Ability to work effectively with students of different ages and skill levels. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Energetic, creative, dependable, and engaging. Ability to take direction and work collaboratively with lead instructors and School of Dance staff. Strong organizational skills and attention to student safety. Ability to maintain a positive and professional attitude. Must be punctual and reliable. Ability and willingness to work primarily during late afternoon and early evening hours. Important Notes: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 10/08/2026 will be given priority consideration. Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please, specifically address the qualifications, competencies and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current resume, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/541": {
      "title": "WS - Facilities Shipping and Receiving Assistant - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Facilities Shipping and Receiving Assistant - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. FACILITIES SHIPPING AND RECEIVING ASSISTANT Division: Support Services Department: Facilities Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSSHIPRECAST Supervisor/Reports To: Jimmy Raines Start Date: 8/25/2026 Assist with shipping, receiving, and delivery of packages and freight on campus. Ideal for students with strong attention to detail and ability to work independently and collaboratively. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Process incoming and outgoing packages and freight – C, TW, P, CT Deliver packages to various campus departments and offices – C, TW, P, CT Update and maintain inventory records – C, P, CT, T Maintain confidentiality and customer service when interacting with campus community – C, TW, P Report problems or discrepancies to supervisor – C, P Adhere to safety procedures and guidelines – P, CT, TW Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Preferred Skills: Word, Excel, attention to detail, customer service, written and verbal communication. Work Schedule: Monday–Friday, 8 AM – 5 PM (hours flexible based on student schedule). Work Conditions: Indoor/outdoor work; exposure to heat, cold, dust, and noise. Physical Demands: Reaching/handling, stooping/kneeling, pushing/pulling/lifting/carrying up to 50 lbs. Number of Positions: 1 Pay Rate: $8.75/hour Location: Shipping/Receiving (HPE 103) To Apply: Complete application and upload resume. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
