    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/542": {
      "title": "WS - Communications Teaching Assistant - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Communications Teaching Assistant - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. Communications Teaching Assistant Division: CAS Department: Communications Experience: Advanced Job Code: NA Supervisor of Student Employee(s): Chandra Massner Requested Start Date: 8 26/2026 Assist the Communication program with clerical, academic, and research support duties. Maintain confidentiality, support projects, and provide classroom assistance as needed. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Maintain confidentiality including FERPA, be punctual, and communicate schedule changes in advance – L, P Provide clerical support including proofreading, photocopying, filing, and assigned projects – TW Use superior verbal and written communication, especially APA writing style – C, CT Use MS Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and compile data using software programs – T Assist with development of course resources – T, C, CT Work independently and efficiently; guide students using available resources – CT, P, L Prioritize responsibilities and meet deadlines – L, CT Be available to assist in class as a TA, including monitoring exams – L, P, CT Dress appropriately for the work environment – P Monitor and post to social media accounts – P, T, CSD Grade assignments as directed by faculty, -- T, CT, P, CTR Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) In the following sections check all boxes that apply to your job. Computer Skills: Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Social Media Other Skills: Attention to detail, Classroom speaking on occasion, Written & verbal communication, Willingness to learn new things Work Schedule: M-F 9-5 hours may vary depending on workload Work Conditions: Light Intensity Physical Demands: Keyboarding, Reaching/Handling, Lifting up to 10 lbs., Carrying up to 10 lbs., Number of Positions: 1 Hours needed per week: 10 Pay Rate: $10.50/hour Location: Armington 4th floor Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
