    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/544": {
      "title": "WS - Intramural Sports Game Day Official",
      "description": "WS - Intramural Sports Game Day Official. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. CSE INTRAMURAL SPORTS GAME DAY OFFICIAL Division: Support Services Department: CSE Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSCSEINTRMLOF Supervisor/Reports To: Tyler Freas Start Date: 8/25/2026 Support the CSE team by officiating intramural sports competitions and maintaining a respectful environment. Ensure rule enforcement and safety while collaborating with game day staff. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Serve as the referee or umpire for intramural sports events – C, TW, P, T Make accurate and unbiased calls according to the rules of the game – C, TW, P, CTR, L Ensure the safety of all participants by monitoring play and enforcing rules – C, L, P, CT Understand and apply the official rules and regulations for each sport – C, TW, P, CTR, L Address rule violations and disputes promptly and fairly – C, TW, P, CTR, L Ensure games start and end on time – C, TW, P, CT, L Monitor playing area and equipment for safety hazards – C, L, P, CT Communicate clearly with players, coaches, and officials – C, TW, P, CTR, L Maintain accurate game records and submit reports – C, TW, P, CSD, CTR, L Participate in training sessions and support fellow officials – C, TW, P, CSD, CTR, L Competencies/Skills: Career & Self-Development (CSD), Communication (C), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Professionalism (P), Teamwork (TW), Technology (T) Education Requirements: Must be enrolled and in good academic standing at UPIKE. Preferred Skills: Organization, interpersonal skills, stress management, multitasking, sports knowledge. Work Schedule: Sunday through Saturday; hours vary based on sport schedule. Work Conditions: Heat, cold, outdoor exposure. Physical Demands: Standing for long periods, movement on fields, lifting light equipment. Number of Positions: Multiple, flexible hours per week (4–8 depending on sport) Pay Rate: $8.75/hour Location: Campus locations including Bob Amos and Bear Mountain To Apply: Submit required application sections, resume, and class schedule. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/545": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Dean of Post-Graduate Education",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Dean of Post-Graduate Education. Department: Kentucky College of Optometry. Full-Time. The Assistant/Associate Dean of Postgraduate Education provides strategic leadership for the Kentucky College of Optometry's lifelong learning mission by overseeing educational opportunities that extend beyond graduation and throughout a graduate's professional career. Serving as the Institutional Residency Director, the Assistant Dean provides leadership for residency and fellowship programs, continuing education, postdoctoral training, alumni professional development, and graduate success initiatives. The Assistant Dean works collaboratively with academic, clinical, and administrative leadership to develop innovative educational pathways that prepare graduates for advanced clinical practice, leadership, academia, and lifelong professional growth. The position fosters strong partnerships with residency affiliates, professional organizations, alumni, and University graduate programs while ensuring compliance with accreditation standards and advancing the College's strategic priorities. Mission of the Office of Postgraduate Education The Office of Postgraduate Education advances the Kentucky College of Optometry's commitment to lifelong learning by supporting graduates through advanced clinical training, continuing professional education, leadership development, alumni engagement, and educational innovation. The Office fosters a culture of continuous professional growth while strengthening the College's impact on the profession and the communities its graduates serve. Residency and Fellowship Programs •Serve as the Institutional Residency Director for all affiliated residency and fellowship programs. •Maintain ACOE residency accreditation, including self-studies, annual reports, substantive changes, and continuous quality improvement. Provide leadership and support to residency coordinators across affiliated training sites. •Lead recruitment, onboarding, orientation, assessment, and evaluation of residents. •Develop policies, curricula, assessment processes, and program outcomes. •Identify and develop new residency and fellowship opportunities. •Collaborate with Academic Affairs and Clinical Education to ensure alignment with institutional goals. Lifelong Learning and Continuing Professional Education •Provide strategic leadership for the College's continuing education program. •Develop an annual calendar of COPE-approved educational offerings. •Collaborate with faculty, alumni, professional organizations, and industry partners. •Ensure compliance with COPE standards. •Expand hybrid, virtual, and in-person educational offerings. Postdoctoral Education and Professional Development •Develop certificate programs, fellowships, leadership academies, faculty development initiatives, and advanced clinical training opportunities. •Serve as liaison with the University's MBA and Master of Biomedical Sciences programs to create collaborative educational opportunities. •Develop pathways that prepare future faculty through leadership, research, teaching, business, and administrative training. •Encourage scholarly activity through mentorship, collaborative research, presentations, and publications. •Develop external partnerships and pursue funding opportunities supporting postgraduate education. Alumni Success and Graduate Support •Develop board preparation, remediation, mentoring, and graduate support initiatives. •Monitor graduate outcomes and board performance trends. •Promote alumni engagement through continuing education, networking, and leadership opportunities. •Collaborate with Academic Affairs to use graduate outcomes to strengthen the curriculum. Strategic Leadership •Develop and implement the strategic vision for postgraduate education. •Represent the College through participation in regional, national, and international professional organizations. •Develop partnerships with residency affiliates, healthcare organizations, alumni, and professional societies. •Participate in accreditation, assessment, and strategic planning initiatives. •Develop and manage budgets related to postgraduate education and continuing education. •Serve on College and University committees as assigned. Reporting Relationships •Reports to the Dean of the Kentucky College of Optometry. •Supervises residency coordinators, residents, continuing education personnel (as assigned), and other staff within the Office of Postgraduate Education. •Maintains an active faculty appointment with teaching, scholarship, and/or clinical responsibilities as assigned. Required Qualifications •Doctor of Optometry (OD) degree from an accredited college or school of optometry. •Completion of an accredited optometric residency. •Minimum of seven (7) years of progressively responsible experience in academic optometry, Veterans Affairs (VA) optometric practice, military optometric practice, or a combination thereof, including demonstrated educational leadership and administrative responsibilities. •Experience in postgraduate education, residency training, continuing education, or academic leadership. •Eligibility for Kentucky licensure. •Excellent communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. •Commitment to lifelong learning and the mission of KYCO. Preferred Qualifications •Experience as a residency director or comparable postgraduate education leader. •Experience supervising faculty, staff, or educational programs. •Knowledge of ACOE residency accreditation standards. •Knowledge of COPE accreditation standards. •Experience with accreditation, assessment, and continuous quality improvement. •Record of scholarly activity and leadership in professional organizations. Application review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 9/21/2026 will be given priority consideration. Important Notes: Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please specifically address the qualifications, competencies, and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living, and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check and, when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current resume, and contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/547": {
      "title": "Executive Director of KYCO Clinics",
      "description": "Executive Director of KYCO Clinics. Department: Kentucky College of Optometry. Full-Time. The Executive Director of KYCO Clinics provides executive leadership for the Kentucky College of Optometry's (KYCO) clinical enterprise, advancing the College's mission to develop leaders in therapeutic optometry through innovative education and a commitment to caring for the underserved. The position is responsible for the strategic growth, operational excellence, financial sustainability, and continuous advancement of KYCO Clinics while ensuring exceptional patient care and meaningful clinical education experiences. Working collaboratively with the Dean, Assistant Dean of Clinical Education, faculty, University leadership, and community partners, the Executive Director leads the administrative, operational, and strategic functions of the clinical enterprise. This executive role strengthens community partnerships, expands access to care, supports innovative models of healthcare delivery, and ensures that clinical operations provide the infrastructure necessary for outstanding patient care, student learning, and future multidisciplinary growth. Responsibilities Lead the strategic direction and day-to-day administration of the KYCO’s clinical enterprise across all university-operated clinics and affiliated clinical education sites. Develop operational priorities, performance expectations, and key performance indicators that guide patient access, operational efficiency, financial performance, educational capacity, and quality outcomes. Maintain the KYCO Clinics Policy and Procedure Manual, ensuring compliance with University policies, Accreditation Council on Optometric Education (ACOE) standards, and applicable regulatory requirements. Develop and implement operational policies, procedures, and workflows that promote consistency, accountability, and exceptional patient care. Provide the Dean with regular reports and recommendations regarding clinical performance, opportunities for growth, and operational improvement. Direct initiatives that strengthen patient access, referral relationships, and sustainable growth of the clinical enterprise. Serve as the primary administrative liaison with Pikeville Medical Center, Federally Qualified Health Centers, private practice affiliates, and other clinical partners. Develop, negotiate, and maintain affiliation agreements and memoranda of understanding supporting patient care and clinical education. Collaborate with Marketing and Communications to promote clinical services, referral development, patient outreach, and community engagement. Identify opportunities for new services, partnerships, and multidisciplinary collaboration that align with the College's mission. Oversee clinic budgets, financial performance, payor strategy, operational metrics, and resource utilization. Partner with Finance and revenue cycle personnel to improve reimbursement, coding, collections, and operational efficiency. Evaluate provider productivity, scheduling, patient flow, fill rates, no-show trends, and service-line performance to guide operational decisions. Use data and analytics to support informed decision-making, continuous improvement, and long-term sustainability. Lead quality improvement, patient safety, and regulatory compliance initiatives across the clinical enterprise. Ensure compliance with HIPAA, OSHA, payer requirements, University policies, and ACOE expectations. Oversee facility planning, equipment replacement, preventive maintenance, and capital improvement planning to support exceptional patient care and education. Provide strategic leadership and supervision for the Clinic Operations Manager, Clinical Coordinator, and assigned administrative personnel. Partner with the Assistant Dean of Clinical Education to ensure clinical operations effectively support the educational mission of the College. Collaborate with University departments including Finance, Human Resources, Information Technology, Facilities, Compliance, and Marketing and Communications. Partner with academic leadership to integrate contemporary practice management, healthcare leadership, and clinical operations into the student experience. Foster a culture of innovation, accountability, service, collaboration, and continuous improvement Other duties as assigned Education Master's degree in Healthcare Administration, Business Administration, Public Health, Healthcare Management, or a closely related field. Experience Minimum of seven (7) years of progressively responsible healthcare leadership Demonstrated experience in healthcare operations, budgeting, strategic planning, personnel supervision, and regulatory compliance. Exceptional leadership, communication, analytical, and relationship-building skills Preferred Qualifications Professional certification such as FACHE, FACMPE, CMPE, CHC, CPHQ, or equivalent. Experience in an academic health center or health professions education environment. Experience with multisite ambulatory care, FQHCs, Rural Health Clinics, or health system partnerships. Knowledge of optometric practice operations and ACOE accreditation. Application review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 9/30/2026 will be given priority consideration. Important Notes: Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please specifically address the qualifications, competencies, and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living, and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check and, when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current resume, and contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/548": {
      "title": "Research Associate / Laboratory Manager",
      "description": "Research Associate / Laboratory Manager. Department: Academic Affairs. Full-Time. The University of Pikeville seeks a Research Associate / Laboratory Manager to support an NIH-funded molecular biotechnology research program focused on plant-based production and characterization of recombinant therapeutic proteins. The successful candidate will conduct molecular biology and plant biotechnology research, assist with recombinant protein expression and analysis, manage daily laboratory operations, and train undergraduate student researchers. Responsibilities • Conduct molecular biology and biotechnology experiments supporting the NIH R15 project. • Perform cloning, PCR, gel electrophoresis, bacterial culture, recombinant DNA procedures, and plant expression. • Maintain plants and process samples for recombinant protein extraction and analysis. • Perform plant transformation, SDS-PAGE, Western blotting, ELISA, protein quantification, and related assays. • Collect, analyze, and document experimental data. • Manage daily laboratory operations, supplies, inventories, purchasing, equipment, reagents, and records. • Maintain SOPs and laboratory safety and compliance documentation. • Train and supervise undergraduate researchers in laboratory techniques, experiments, data collection, and research documentation. • Assist with research reports, presentations, posters, and manuscripts. • Support IBC, biosafety, chemical safety, and waste-disposal requirements • Other duties as assigned. Education • Bachelor’s degree in molecular biology, biology, biotechnology, biochemistry, biomedical science, or a related field. • Master’s or Ph.D. degree in molecular biology, biotechnology, biochemistry, plant biology, biomedical science, or a related field. Experience • Hands-on laboratory experience in molecular biology or a related discipline. • Experience with basic techniques such as PCR, DNA purification, gel electrophoresis, bacterial culture, or recombinant DNA methods. • Strong organizational, communication, and laboratory-recordkeeping skills. • Ability to work independently and collaboratively with faculty and undergraduate researchers. • Experience with recombinant protein expression, molecular cloning, SDS-PAGE, Western blotting, ELISA, or protein purification. • Experience managing laboratory operations or training undergraduate researchers. • Familiarity with biosafety, IBC, or NIH-funded research environments. Application review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 9/28/2026 will be given priority consideration. Important Notes: Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please specifically address the qualifications, competencies, and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living, and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check and, when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current resume, and contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/549": {
      "title": "General Dentist",
      "description": "General Dentist. Department: Tanner College Dental Medicine. Full-Time. The General Dentist will provide comprehensive dental care through the College’s faculty practice and/or direct supervision of student-delivered care, with a commitment to serving vulnerable and underserved populations consistent with the College’s mission. The position will participate in interprofessional education and collaboration with UPIKE health professions programs and contribute to integrated care models that promote best practices in interdisciplinary health professions education. The General Dentist will also participate in departmental committees, curriculum review, student assessment, and institutional initiatives, including CODA accreditation preparation, continuous quality improvement, and strategic planning. The position will contribute to community outreach efforts that address oral health disparities and improve access to care in rural Appalachian communities. The General Dentist will engage in scholarship or community-based inquiry related to general dentistry, oral health disparities, or dental education, while pursuing ongoing professional development and continuing education to remain current in advances in clinical practice and dental education. Responsibilities: Supervise predoctoral dental students in the diagnosis, comprehensive treatment planning, and delivery of restorative, endodontic, prosthodontic, and oral surgical procedures within clinical settings. Model exemplary patient-centered care and ethical and professional conduct in compliance with established standards. Integrate digital dentistry tools and contemporary clinical technologies into student supervision and instruction. Create learning materials, facilitate seminars, and lead small-group discussions in general dentistry and related biomedical and clinical sciences. Develop and refine curriculum content in alignment with Commission on Dental Accreditation (CODA) standards and the College’s curricular goals. Incorporate evidence-based practice and interprofessional perspectives into all instructional activities. Serve as a mentor and professional role model, providing constructive, timely feedback on student performance and clinical competency. Provide comprehensive dental care to patients within the College’s faculty practice or through direct supervision of student-delivered care. Demonstrate a commitment to serving vulnerable and underserved patient populations consistent with the College’s mission. Actively participate in interprofessional education initiatives in collaboration with UPIKE’s programs in medicine, optometry, nursing, and social work. Contribute to the development of integrated care models that reflect best practices in interdisciplinary health professions education. Engage in CODA accreditation preparation, continuous quality improvement efforts, and institutional strategic planning. Contribute to community outreach initiatives addressing oral health disparities in rural Appalachian communities. Pursue and maintain continuing education to remain current with advances in clinical practice and dental pedagogy. Requirements: DMD or DDS degree from a CODA-accredited institution or equivalent. Possess or be eligible to obtain a license to practice dentistry in Kentucky or faculty-limited licensure. Graduate of a CODA-accredited GPR/AEGD program is preferred. Previous experience supervising predoctoral dental education students at CODA-accredited institutions and/or familiarity with community dentistry, Federally Qualified Health Centers (FQHCs), or rural health practice environments is preferred. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of comprehensive dental diagnosis, treatment planning, and clinical procedures in restorative dentistry, endodontics, prosthodontics, and oral surgery. Ability to effectively supervise and instruct predoctoral dental students in clinical settings. Ability to model patient-centered care and ethical and professional conduct. Knowledge of digital dentistry tools and contemporary clinical technologies. Ability to create learning materials, facilitate seminars, and lead small-group discussions. Knowledge of evidence-based dental practice and interprofessional education. Ability to provide constructive and timely feedback on student performance and clinical competency. Ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, students, and other health professions programs. Commitment to serving vulnerable and underserved populations and improving access to oral healthcare in rural Appalachian communities. Ability to participate in curriculum development, CODA accreditation activities, continuous quality improvement, and institutional strategic planning. The University of Pikeville offers a competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. UPIKE offers a competitive benefits package including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance, telemedicine, long term disability, tuition waivers, a 403(b)-retirement plan, and HSA, FSA, & dependent care accounts. UPIKE also offers a generous holiday schedule and paid leave program. Important Notes: Application review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 10/16/2026 will be given priority consideration. Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please, specifically address the qualifications, competencies and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, copies of their transcripts, a teaching philosophy statement, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/550": {
      "title": "Part-Time Assistant Women's Basketball Coach",
      "description": "Part-Time Assistant Women's Basketball Coach. Department: Women's Basketball. Part-Time. The University of Pikeville in Pikeville, Kentucky, is seeking an innovative professional for the position of Part-time Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach within the Athletic Department. This is an exceptional opportunity for a motivated and accomplished leader to join an innovative Athletic Department valuing academic and out-of-classroom experiences. The Part-time Assistant Women’s Basketball Coach will report to the Head Women’s Basketball Coach. Responsibilities Administrative duties in all phases of the program. Assist with all phases of competitive NAIA-compliant recruiting. Ability to produce game-day and recruiting graphics. Evaluate prospective student-athletes through games, showcases, and video observation. Execute and evaluate practice and game planning, including video Directly responsible for position skill development in assigned area(s). Practice planning and implementation. Assist with the direction of camps, fundraising, and other program development activities. Scheduling: Assist with arranging aspects of team travel including but not limited to team meals for home and away contests and team lodging arrangements. Assist the Head Coach with office and administrative duties. Ability to help coach and lead the program’s junior varsity program. Recruiting athletically and academically qualified students. Retaining students in the program. Responsible for understanding the expectations of the Athletic Department. Provide for the safety of students and coaches, facilities, and equipment while conducting activities, practices, and competitions. Regularly attend and participate in department meetings and professional development opportunities. Collaborate with campus constituents to assess, provide, and improve student experience related to Women's Basketball. Understand the culture of the Women's Basketball program, athletic department, and the campus. Understand the NAIA eligibility rules. Operate university vehicles. Other Duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree Required. Must be able to follow the vision of the Program. Must be able to work under challenging conditions and with others. Willing to work late/flexible hours. Excellent English communication skills, both written and oral. Ability to work with others and lead. Demonstrate sensitivity to students with diverse academic, socio-economic, cultural, and ethnic backgrounds, including those with disabilities. Understand how to work successfully as a team within all levels of the organization and know how to contribute to the mission of the university. Important Notes: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 10/01/2026 will be given priority consideration. Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please specifically address the qualifications, competencies, and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living, and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check and, when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current resume, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/552": {
      "title": "Director of Simulation, Innovation, and Research",
      "description": "Director of Simulation, Innovation, and Research. Department: Tanner College Dental Medicine. Full-Time. The Tanner College of Dental Medicine (TCDM) is seeking an open-rank, full-time faculty leadership position to serve as the Director of Simulation, Innovation, and Research. The Director of Director of Simulation, Innovation, and Research will advance simulation-based education, educational innovation, and scholarly activity across the College, with primary responsibility for teaching and advancing preclinical simulation education in restorative dentistry. This position will provide leadership in the development, implementation, assessment, and continuous improvement of simulation-based learning experiences throughout the DMD curriculum. Working collaboratively with course directors, faculty, academic leadership, Associate Deans, and other University partners, the Director will identify and implement innovative approaches to dental education, including the appropriate use of emerging technologies, digital dentistry, artificial intelligence, simulation, and other evidence-based educational methodologies. The Director will also maintain an active program of scholarly activity and contribute to faculty and student scholarship in coordination with the Associate Dean of Research. Primary Responsibilities: Preclinical and Simulation-Based Education Teach assigned preclinical simulation courses, with primary responsibility for restorative dentistry. Provide direct instruction, demonstration, supervision, and feedback in foundational and advanced restorative dentistry procedures and techniques. Participate in the development and delivery of a vertically and horizontally integrated restorative dentistry curriculum. Develop simulation-based learning experiences that support competency development, clinical reasoning, psychomotor skills, treatment planning, and clinical readiness. Develop and implement competency-based exercises, practical examinations, and other assessments of student performance. Provide individualized feedback, remediation, and academic support to students requiring additional assistance in achieving preclinical competencies. Participate in faculty calibration to promote consistency in instruction, assessment, grading, and remediation. Collaborate with course directors and faculty to ensure appropriate integration of simulation experiences across the DMD curriculum. Incorporate contemporary restorative materials, digital workflows, CAD/CAM, 3D printing, and other relevant technologies into preclinical education, as appropriate. Contribute to the evaluation and continuous improvement of preclinical and simulation-based courses. Simulation Program Leadership Provide faculty leadership for the development and continuous improvement of TCDM’s simulation-based educational program. Collaborate with academic leadership and faculty to establish and maintain a comprehensive simulation strategy aligned with the College’s competency-based curriculum. Evaluate simulation methodologies and technologies for their educational effectiveness and relevance to student learning. Promote effective and innovative use of haptic simulation, digital simulation, virtual and augmented reality, and other emerging simulation technologies. Develop opportunities to use simulation for clinical readiness, remediation, assessment, interdisciplinary learning, and continuing education. Establish and promote best practices for simulation instruction, student feedback, faculty calibration, and competency assessment. Work with appropriate faculty and staff to optimize the use of simulation facilities, equipment, software, and educational resources. Serve as a faculty resource for colleagues seeking to incorporate simulation into their courses. Educational Innovation Lead faculty-level initiatives focused on innovation in teaching, learning, assessment, and clinical preparation. Identify and evaluate emerging educational technologies and methodologies that have the potential to enhance student learning. Support thoughtful and evidence-based applications of artificial intelligence in dental education. Promote innovative applications of digital dentistry, CAD/CAM, 3D printing, and other technologies within the curriculum. Develop and evaluate pilot educational initiatives and disseminate successful approaches throughout TCDM. Serve as a faculty champion for experimentation, evaluation, and continuous improvement in dental education. Facilitate faculty development related to simulation, innovative teaching methodologies, emerging technologies, and educational assessment. Scholarly Activity and Research Collaboration Maintain an active program of scholarly activity consistent with faculty appointment and rank. Conduct and disseminate scholarly work related to simulation-based education, restorative dentistry, dental materials, digital dentistry, educational innovation, emerging technologies, or other areas of professional expertise. Mentor students and faculty in scholarly projects, presentations, publications, and other academic activities. Collaborate with the Associate Dean of Research and other faculty investigators on research projects aligned with TCDM priorities. Contribute to the development of research and scholarly proposals, when appropriate. Participate in peer-reviewed publications, professional presentations, research conferences, and other scholarly activities. Support opportunities for students to engage in research, innovation, and scholarly activities. Contribute to a culture of scholarly inquiry and evidence-based educational practice within TCDM. Collaboration with CRET and Other Innovation Initiatives Collaborate with the Director of the CRET Innovation Center on appropriate educational innovation initiatives. Contribute expertise in simulation, digital dentistry, restorative dentistry, and emerging educational technologies to interdisciplinary projects. Support the evaluation of technologies and educational innovations that may be relevant to CRET initiatives. Participate in collaborative projects when they align with the Director’s academic and educational responsibilities. Faculty and Student Development Mentor students in preclinical restorative dentistry and simulation-based learning. Provide faculty development in simulation instruction, competency-based assessment, restorative dentistry, digital dentistry, and educational innovation. Serve as a resource for faculty developing innovative learning experiences. Encourage student participation in research, innovation, scholarly presentations, and professional activities. Participate in student advising, mentoring, and other faculty responsibilities as assigned. Assessment and Continuous Improvement Establish and monitor measures of effectiveness for simulation-based learning. Analyze student performance and assessment data to identify opportunities for improvement in preclinical education. Collaborate with course directors and academic leadership on continuous quality improvement. Evaluate the effectiveness of new simulation technologies and educational innovations before and after implementation. Contribute to curriculum review, program assessment, accreditation activities, and strategic planning, as appropriate. Faculty Responsibilities As a faculty member of TCDM, the Director will: Teach assigned preclinical and simulation-based restorative dentistry courses. Participate in course and curriculum development. Participate in student assessment, grading, calibration, remediation, and academic advising, as assigned. Participate in faculty meetings, committees, and institutional activities. Maintain professional development and scholarly activity appropriate to faculty rank. Participate in accreditation and quality improvement activities. Contribute to the academic and professional life of TCDM. Minimum Qualifications DMD or DDS from a CODA-accredited institution, or equivalent dental degree. Demonstrated experience teaching preclinical, simulation-based, restorative, or prosthodontic dental education. Demonstrated experience in restorative dentistry and/or prosthodontics. Evidence of scholarly activity, such as peer-reviewed publications, presentations, research projects, or other scholarly contributions. Demonstrated interest or experience in educational innovation, simulation, digital dentistry, or emerging technologies. Strong interpersonal, communication, organizational, and collaborative skills. Kentucky dental license or eligibility for a Kentucky dental license or faculty-limited license. Preferred Qualifications Advanced training or graduate education in prosthodontics, restorative dentistry, dental education, dental materials, or a related discipline. Experience directing or coordinating preclinical or simulation-based dental courses. Experience with competency-based dental education and assessment. Experience with digital dentistry, CAD/CAM, 3D printing, dental materials, or related technologies. Experience incorporating artificial intelligence or other emerging technologies into dental education. Demonstrated record of scholarly productivity. Experience mentoring students or faculty in scholarly activities. Demonstrated leadership in simulation education or educational innovation. The University of Pikeville offers a competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. UPIKE offers a competitive benefits package including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance, telemedicine, long term disability, tuition waivers, a 403(b)-retirement plan, and HSA, FSA, & dependent care accounts. UPIKE also offers a generous holiday schedule and paid leave program. Important Notes: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 10/17/2026 will be given priority consideration. Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please, specifically address the qualifications, competencies and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, copies of their transcripts, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/554": {
      "title": "WS - Center for Public Service Policy Analyst - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Center for Public Service Policy Analyst - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. Center for Public Service Policy Analyst Division: Social Science Department: Political Science Experience: Entry-level Job Code: Supervisor / Reports To : Dr. Tyler Syck Internship Window: Fall or Spring Semester Location: University of Pikeville | Center for Public Service | 147 Sycamore St. Pikeville, KY The Policy Analyst Intern will support the Center for Public Service's research and policy initiatives, with particular emphasis on understanding and addressing the economic, civic, and social challenges facing Appalachia. This internship provides hands-on experience in policy research, statistical analysis, and report writing. Interns will work closely with Center leadership while gaining practical exposure to careers in public policy, research, and regional development. Internship Duties, Responsibilities, and Career Competencies: Research and analyze economic, civic, and demographic trends affecting Appalachian communities. (CT, CTR) Draft policy reports and briefs on issues such as economic development, education, healthcare access, and civic infrastructure in the region. (C, CT, CSD) Collect, clean, and analyze quantitative and qualitative data using standard statistical tools. (CT, T) Assist the Director in preparing testimony, white papers, and briefing materials for policymakers and partner organizations. (C, CT, P) Support research for the Center's fellowship and programmatic initiatives, including the Allegheny Civic Fellowship. (TW, CSD, CTR) Conduct literature reviews and synthesize existing research on rural and Appalachian policy issues. (CT, CSD) Help design data visualizations, charts, and summaries to communicate findings to general and academic audiences. (C, CT, T) Assist the Director and Program Associate in researching and drafting grant proposals related to policy and research initiatives. (CT, CSD, P) Competencies / Skills Developed: Communication (C) · Teamwork (TW) · Professionalism (P) · Career & Self Development (CSD) · Critical Thinking (CT) · Community Transformation (CTR) · Leadership (L) · Technology (T) Other Skills: Strong analytical and quantitative reasoning abilities. Clear, precise writing suited to policy and research audiences. Interest in Appalachian studies, public policy, and regional development. Comfort working both independently and collaboratively on research projects. Work Schedule: Flexible scheduling coordinated with the Director and Program Associate. Hours will vary depending on research deadlines and program needs. Number of Positions: 1 Pay Rate: Beginning at $8.75/hour Location: Armington Learning Center University of Pikeville | Center for Public Service | 147 Sycamore St. Pikeville, KY Additional Comments: Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/555": {
      "title": "WS - Center for Public Service Program Assistant - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Center for Public Service Program Assistant - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. INTERNSHIP – Center for Public Service Program Assistant Division: Social Science Department: Political Science Experience: Entry-level Job Code: Supervisor / Reports To : Dr. Tyler Syck) Terms : Fall or Spring Semester Location: University of Pikeville | Center for Public Service | 147 Sycamore St. Pikeville, KY The Program Assistant Intern will support the daily operations and major initiatives of the Center for Public Service, with particular emphasis on civic education programming and preparation for the Allegheny Civic Fellowship summer institute. This position provides hands-on experience in nonprofit administration, event planning, civic programming, communications, and grant development. Interns will work closely with Center leadership while gaining practical exposure to careers in public service, education, and community engagement. Organization Description (General): The Center for Public Service at the University of Pikeville is dedicated to cultivating civic leadership, community engagement, and public-spirited scholarship across Eastern Kentucky. Through educational initiatives, fellowships, public programming, and partnerships with local institutions, the Center works to strengthen democratic culture and prepare students for lives of meaningful public contribution. Duties, Responsibilities, and Career Competencies: · Assist the Director and Program Associate in planning events and managing the Allegheny Civic Fellowship. (C, TW, L, CSD) · Generate original content for the Center for Public Service’s social media platforms to promote civic initiatives and programming. (C, CT, T) · Help coordinate and manage the Director’s schedule, including meetings, events, and public engagements. (C, P, CSD) · Answer phones and assist with general office communication and outreach. (C, P) · Create engaging instructional and promotional content for the Civics Summer Camp. (C, CT, T) · Assist in compiling primary source documents and educational resources for local K–12 educators. (CT, CSD, CTR) · Work with the Director to conduct community outreach regarding civic programming and public events. (C, TW, CTR, L) · Support the Director and Program Associate in researching and drafting grant proposals. (CT, CSD, P) Competencies / Skills Developed: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Qualifications: Current UPIKE student in good academic standing. Interest in public service, civic education, political science, history, communications, or related fields. Strong organizational and communication skills preferred. Experience with event planning, social media, or educational programming is helpful but not required. Other Skills: · Strong writing and organizational abilities. · Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously. · Interest in civic life, education, and community engagement. · Comfort working both independently and collaboratively. Work Schedule: Flexible scheduling coordinated with the Director and Program Associate. Hours will vary depending on program needs, particularly during summer Fellowship programming and major civic events. Number of Positions: 1 Pay Rate: Beginning at $8.75/hour Location: Armington Learning Center University of Pikeville | Center for Public Service | 147 Sycamore St. Pikeville, KY Additional Comments: Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/556": {
      "title": "Analyst",
      "description": "Analyst. Department: Vice President Academic Affair. Full-Time. The Institutional Research Analyst is responsible for the collection, analysis, and interpretation of data to support research, planning, assessment, and evidence-based decision-making. This role maintains the data accessibility functions of the institution, coordinating semester and annual reports to aid in compliance with all accreditation agencies, as well as state and federal reporting Responsibilities To maintain a campus-wide, undisputed database of pertinent internal and external data to support institutional decision-making. To collect and disseminate data to all educational and administrative/support services units of the institution for use in institutional effectiveness planning (IEP’s). To aid IEP unit coordinators in the development of educational goals/objectives, design and selection of appropriate assessment tools and criteria, and in the analysis and use of assessment results to improve programs. To aid college institutional effectiveness, long-range, and facilities planning To complete IPEDS and other external reports required for federal, state, and private funding agencies and accrediting groups. To complete internal reports for review by Executive Staff and President’s Cabinet, the administration, and the faculty as needed. To aid in arrangements for campus-wide review of all institutional effectiveness To assist in completion of accrediting and institutional self-study reports and follow- To stay abreast of trends in institutional research, planning, and accreditation and provide workshops and seminars to inform institutional constituents. To perform other tasks and responsibilities as directed by the Relationships The position requires daily contact with executive staff, faculty, staff, and students to compile and disseminate data to support institutional decision-making. These relationships are maintained through e-mail, telephone, and person-to-person contact. Responsibility for Final Decisions Tasks require the development of techniques, formulation of concepts and procedures, direction and/or planning operations, and developing solutions to unique issues. Work involves developing, implementing, and interpreting policy. Problem resolution requires experimentation, innovation, and/or theory development. Reports to VPAA The Data Analyst is directly accountable for program/work unit results, where it is expected that the collection, compilation, and dissemination of data are performed accurately. Education/Skill Requirements Bachelor's degree in Educational Research, Data Science, Statistics, Social Sciences, Computer Science, Public Administration, or related field; Master’s degree preferred. 2-3 years’ experience with data collection, analysis, and report writing in an office of institutional research at an institution of higher education. Experience extracting data from Enterprise Planning Systems (ERPs). Experience with data visualization tools (e.g., Informer, Power BI, Tableau) and knowledge of developing dashboards and reports. The University of Pikeville offers a competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. UPIKE offers a competitive benefits package including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance, telemedicine, long term disability, tuition waivers, a 403(b)-retirement plan, and HSA, FSA, & dependent care accounts. UPIKE also offers a generous holiday schedule and paid leave program. Important Notes: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 10/05/2026 will be given priority consideration. Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please specifically address the qualifications, competencies, and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living, and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check and, when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, copies of their transcripts, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/557": {
      "title": "Assistant Director - Center for Career, Vocation, & Leadership",
      "description": "Assistant Director - Center for Career, Vocation, & Leadership. Department: Ctr Career/Vocation/Lead. Full-Time. The University of Pikeville is seeking qualified candidates for the position of a grant-funded Assistant Director within the Center for Career, Vocation, & Leadership. The Assistant Director for the Center for Career, Vocation, & Leadership is responsible for the strategic oversight and operational management of the college's student engagement initiative (First Year/Second Year Experience, Admissions, employer/student engagement), with a primary focus on supporting the function of career preparation programming at the University of Pikeville. This position will play a pivotal role in enhancing student career development by fostering meaningful skill-building experiences that align with academic goals and industry needs. Responsibilities: Partner with campus units such as student success, alumni relations, admissions, advancement, intercultural programs, counseling center, residence life, international education, First-Year Experience, new student orientation (GROWL), and financial aid to support career-related initiatives across campus. Plan and deliver educational programming related to career, vocation, and leadership with students. Collaborate with campus partners to advance the vocation initiative at UPIKE. Assist students and other constituents with job search, employment skill development, and professionalism as needed. Oversee planning of campus visits, career fairs, campus Career Travel project, etc. Engage with community partners and stakeholders to assist in directing career-ready programming. Collaborate with Community Engagement and Campus Employment to ensure students are ready to begin internship placements. Direct data-informed decision-making with strong analytical capabilities. Oversee management of career services software (e.g., Handshake, Symplicity) and CRM tools. Develop results-driven strategies focused on continuous program improvement and impact reporting. Provide career counseling and advising to students regarding internship opportunities, career goals, and professional development. Assist students in developing professional skills, such as resume writing, interviewing, and networking. Offer guidance on academic planning and career pathways. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in higher education, counseling, communications, or a related field; master’s preferred. Proven experience in career services, student engagement, or related fields. Strong understanding of student development and career supports. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, both written and verbal. Strong organizational and project management skills. Proficiency in data analysis and reporting. Ability to work independently and collaboratively. Passion for student success and career development. This is a full-time position with competitive compensation and benefits. This position is ideal for an energetic higher education professional who thrives on cross-campus collaboration, student mentorship, and data-driven strategy implementation. The best candidate will seamlessly balance hands-on career advising and event execution with employer networking and data tracking to elevate student career success. Important Notes: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 10/06/2026 will be given priority consideration. Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please, specifically address the qualifications, competencies and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, copies of their transcripts, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/558": {
      "title": "WS - Bio Medical Science Teaching Assistant",
      "description": "WS - Bio Medical Science Teaching Assistant. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. Bio Medical Science Teaching Assistant & Assistant Division: CAS Department: Biology Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSCASBIOASTCR Supervisor/Reports To: Phillip Jen Start Date: Assist with grading for biomedical science undergraduate classes . Ideal for students interested in pursuing education, health sciences or biology careers. Open to any student in any major with attention to detail and accuracy. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Grade laboratory and lecture exams (P,T) Supervise classroom examinations for compliance ( P, C, L) Wash and clean all lab materials and equipment for OSHA compliance – C, TW Help supervise A&P and histology labs – C, P, CSD, TW, CT, T Assist with and contribute to events hosted by departmental staff – C, TW, P Work independently and efficiently; use available resources to direct guests – CT, P Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Preferred Skills: Word, attention to detail, strong active listening abilities, , written & verbal communication, willingness to learn new things. Work Schedule: Weekdays depending on class schedule; occasional weekends if time-sensitive projects arise. Work Conditions: Machinery and Toxic Agents Physical Demands: Number of Positions: 1 - 2 Pay Rate: $10.50/hour Location: ARM 1st floor , 112 and 114 To Apply: Complete required sections and upload your academic and practice schedule, and resume or the Student Employment Application. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/561": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor of Music and Director of Choral Activities",
      "description": "Open Rank Professor of Music and Director of Choral Activities. Department: College of Arts and Sciences. Full-Time. The University of Pikeville (UPIKE) is seeking dynamic, student-centered applicants for a full-time, nine-month faculty appointment as an Open-Rank Professor of Music and Director of Choral Activities within the College of Arts & Sciences beginning in January 2027. Faculty members at UPIKE work closely with students in a collaborative learning environment that values mentorship, innovation, and meaningful engagement both inside and outside the classroom. The College of Arts & Sciences seeks an energetic educator who is passionate about teaching and committed to serving our students. The faculty’s primary responsibility is to provide high-quality vocal instruction for all levels of learning in the UPIKE Music program. Responsibilities: Oversee the University's Concert Choir and Chamber Singers. Teach undergraduate coursework in music education and musicianship. Coordinate the choral/vocal track of the new Bachelor of Arts or Science in Integrated Music Education P-12. Drive vocal program recruitment by building active partnerships with regional P-12 choral directors. Teach applied studio voice lessons and provide academic advising for performing arts candidates. Manage the annual choral performance calendar, program budgets, and vocal scholarships. Collaborate within the music program and engage in institutional service and governance. Qualifications: A minimum of a Master’s degree in Music or a closely related field; a terminal degree is preferred. Demonstrated excellence in choral conducting, rehearsal pedagogy, and vocal ensemble direction. Demonstrated competency as a studio voice instructor capable of teaching healthy vocal technique. Functional keyboard/piano accompaniment skills adequate for choral rehearsal, warm-ups, and vocal coaching. Must maintain a valid driver's license for travel associated with recruitment, tours, and clinic adjudications. Minimum level of English: C1 (Common European Language Framework). Important Notes: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 10/31/2026 will be given priority consideration. Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please specifically address the qualifications, competencies, and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living, and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check and, when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, copies of their transcripts, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/563": {
      "title": "Clinical Support Associate-PIKEVILLE",
      "description": "Clinical Support Associate-PIKEVILLE. Department: Kentucky College of Optometry. Full-Time. The University of Pikeville (UPIKE), Kentucky College of Optometry (KYCO), is currently seeking an experienced individual for the position of Clinical Support Associate. This individual will coordinate the operation of the KYCO Eye Clinics and provide administrative support to the Clinical Operations Manager. Responsibilities: Serves patients by greeting and helping them; scheduling appointments; maintaining records and accounts. Welcomes patients and visitors, in person or on the telephone, answering or referring inquiries. Optimizes patients' satisfaction, provider time, and treatment room utilization by scheduling appointments in person or by telephone. Keeps patient appointments on schedule by notifying provider of patient's arrival; reviewing service delivery compared to schedule; reminding provider of service delays. Comforts patients by anticipating patients' anxieties; answering patients' questions; maintaining a clean and organized reception area. Ensures availability of treatment information by filing and retrieving patient records. Maintains patient accounts by obtaining, recording, and updating personal, insurance, and financial information. Obtains revenue by recording and updating financial information; recording and collecting patient charges; controlling credit extended to patients; filing, collecting, and expediting third-party claims. Maintains business office inventory and supplies by checking stock to determine inventory level; anticipating needed supplies; placing and expediting orders for supplies; verifying receipt of supplies; scheduling equipment service and repairs. Helps patients in distress by responding to emergencies. Protects patients’ rights by maintaining confidentiality of personal, financial, and health care information. Maintains operations by following policies and procedures; reporting needed changes. Contributes to team effort by accomplishing related results as needed. Demonstrates professional behavior and appearance. Other duties as assigned by administration. Stay up to date with changes to the electronic medical record system and make adjustments when necessary Must be able to multitask and have flexibility, customer and quality focused, and detail-oriented. Maintain scheduling and strong time management skills. Must be self-motivated and dependable. Education/Skill Requirements: High school diploma or GED; experience in an eye care practice setting preferred. Must have excellent organizational, communication, and decision-making skills. Must be able to multitask, have flexibility, be customer and quality-focused, be detail-oriented, maintain scheduling, and have strong time management skills. Must maintain a high level of professionalism with strong telephone etiquette. Strong computer knowledge, i.e., Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, etc. The University of Pikeville offers a competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. UPIKE offers a competitive benefits package including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance, telemedicine, long-term disability, tuition waivers, a 403(b) retirement plan, and HSA, FSA, & dependent care accounts. UPIKE also offers a generous holiday schedule and paid leave program. Important Notes: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 10/14/2026 will be given priority consideration. Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please specifically address the qualifications, competencies, and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living, and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check and, when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, copies of their transcripts, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/564": {
      "title": "WS - Spring Term INTERNSHIP - Biology Agricultural Research Technologist - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Spring Term INTERNSHIP - Biology Agricultural Research Technologist - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. Biology Agricultural Research Technologist Division: Academic Affairs/CVL Department: Career Pathways Experience: Intermediate Job Code: GL Code: FWS Supervisor of Student Employee(s): Angela Lockhart / Annie Wang FWS, IWS, or Grant Funded: ☒ FWS, ☐ IWS, ☐ Grant Funded Avg. Hours/Week: ☐ 1-5, ☒ 6-10, ☐ 11-15, ☐ 16-20 Requested Start Date: 09/01/2026 Term of Position: ☒ Summer, ☒ Fall, ☐ Spring Student interns will oversee various research projects within the natural sciences laboratories. These projects will typically be environmental/agriculturally focused, with a heavy emphasis on mushrooms. However, internship might include more advanced research work in medicinal plant/fungal extracts. Students in this position will be given advanced research and management responsibilities, including advanced data analyzing and performing standardized experiments. This position is ideal for students interested in biological sciences and research experience. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Organize and maintain a clean and working research laboratory: C, TW, P Assist senior research personnel in prepping sterile substrates (agar, grain, etc…): C, TW, P, CSD, CT, L, T Assist with the design and implementation of novel agriculture research projects: C, TW, P, CSD, CT, CTR, L, T Inoculate, incubate, and harvest mushrooms and hydroponic vegetables: C, TW, P, L, T, CSD Oversee Biology Research Technician Work Study employees’ maintenance on hydroponic and mushroom cultivation units: C, TW, T, CSD, L Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Qualifications: Full-time UPIKE student in good academic standing. This position is ideal for junior or senior students interested in biological sciences and research experience who already have extensive research experience and are looking at more of an advanced, supervisory role. In the following sections check all boxes that apply to your job. Computer Skills: ☒ Word, ☒ Excel, ☒ PowerPoint, ☐ Canva, ☐ Social Media & New Technology, ☐ Other: _________________________ Other Skills: ☒ Attention to detail, ☒ Strong active listening abilities, ☒ Public speaking, ☒ Written & verbal communication, ☐ Customer focused, ☒ Willingness to learn new things Work Schedule: ☐ Su ___ to ___; ☐ M ___ to ___; ☐ T ___ to ___; ☐ W ___ to ___; ☐ R ___ to ___; ☐ F ___ to ___; ☐ Sa ___ to ___; ☒ Hours vary depending on workload (Check days that apply, insert hours if set, otherwise, check “Hours vary depending on workload”.) Work Conditions: ☒ Heat, ☒ Cold, ☐ Odors/Smoke, ☐ Toxic Agents, ☐ Dust, ☐ Machinery, ☒ Light Intensity, ☐ Noise, ☐ Vibrations, ☐ Wetness, ☒ Humidity, ☐ Electrical Currents, ☐ Other: _________________________ Physical Demands: ☒ Keyboarding, ☒ Reaching/Handling, ☒ Stooping/Kneeling, ☒ Crouching/Crawling, ☒ Pushing up to 50_ lbs., ☒ Pulling up to 50_ lbs., ☒ Lifting up to _50 lbs., ☒ Carrying up to 50_ lbs., ☐ Climbing, ☐ Balancing, ☐ Other: _________________________ Number of Positions: 1 Pay Rate: 9.75 /hr Location: Building: Armington, Room #: 212 (lab) Additional Comments: Student must work a minimum of 80 hours in the semester. Student must enroll concurrently into CVL 401: Integrated Internship Experience and successfully complete this course. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/565": {
      "title": "WS - Spring Term INTERNSHIP – BEAR Health Clinic – Marketing - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Spring Term INTERNSHIP – BEAR Health Clinic – Marketing - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. BEAR Health Clinic – Marketing - FWS Division: Academic Affairs Department: Career Pathways Experience: Entry Level Supervisor of Student Employee(s) : Angela Lockhart / Damien Cole FWS, IWS, or Grant Funded: ​ ☒ ​ FWS , ​ ☐ ​ IWS, ​ ☐ ​ Grant Funded Avg. Hours/Week: ​ ☒ ​ 1-5, ​ ☐ ​ 6-10, ​ ☐ ​ 11-15, ​ ☐ ​ 16-20 The Marketing and Community Engagement Intern supports BEAR Healthcare Clinic through marketing, social media, community outreach, and research to increase visibility and improve the clinic experience. Responsibilities and Career Competencies Marketing Commit approximately 5 hours weekly , including bi-weekly meetings. (TW, L) Manage approved social media content, schedules, and clinic-day updates. (C, CSD, P, T) Support marketing campaigns, newsletters, events, and promotional materials. (C, CT, CTR, TW, T) Analyze marketing performance and recommend improvements. (CSD, CT) Consulting Research community needs and patient satisfaction. (C, CSD, CT, CTR) Analyze feedback and prepare reports with recommendations. (C, CSD, CT, P, T) Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Qualifications: UPIKE student in good standing, majoring in Communications or Business (Marketing) preferred. In the following sections check all boxes that apply to your job. Computer Skills: ​ ☒ ​ Word, ​ ☒ ​ Excel, ​ ☐ ​ PowerPoint, ​ ☒ ​ Canva, ​ ☒ ​ Social Media & New Technology, ​ ☒ ​ Other: _________________________ Other Skills: ​ ☒ ​ Attention to detail, ​ ☒ ​ Strong active listening abilities, ​ ☒ ​ Public speaking, ​ ☒ ​ Written & verbal communication, ​ ☐ ​ Customer focused, ​ ☒ ​ Willingness to learn new things Work Schedule: ​ ☐ ​ S u ___ to ___; ​ ☐ ​ M ___ to ___; ​ ☐ ​ T ___ to ___; ​ ☐ ​ W ___ to ___; ​ ☐ ​ R ___ to __ _; ​ ☐ ​ F ___ to ___; ​ ☐ ​ S a ___ to ___ ; ​ ☒ ​ Hours vary depending on workload (Check days that apply, insert hours if set, otherwise, check “Hours vary depending on workload ”. ) Work Conditions: ​ ☒ ​ Heat, ​ ☒ ​ Cold, ​ ☐ ​ Odors/Smoke, ​ ☐ ​ Toxic Agents, ​ ☐ ​ Dust, ​ ☐ ​ Machinery, ​ ☒ ​ Light Intensity, ​ ☐ ​ Noise, ​ ☐ ​ Vibrations, ​ ☐ ​ Wetness, ​ ☐ ​ Humidity , ​ ☐ ​ Electrical Currents, ​ ☐ ​ Other: _________________________ Physical Demands: ​ ☒ ​ Keyboarding, ​ ☒ ​ Reaching/Handling, ​ ☒ ​ Stooping/ Kneeling, ​ ☐ ​ Crouching/Crawling, ​ ☐ ​ Pushing up to ___ lbs., ​ ☐ ​ Pulling up to ___ lbs . , ​ ☐ ​ Lifting up to ___ lbs., ​ ☒ ​ Carrying up to _ 25 __ lbs., ​ ☐ ​ Climbing, ​ ☐ ​ Balancing, ​ ☐ ​ Other: _________________________ Number of Positions: 1 Pay Rate: 8.75/hour Location: Building : Coal _, Room #: _ 913 __ Additional Comments: Student must work a minimum of 80 hours in the semester. Student must enroll concurrently into CVL 401: Integrated Internship Experience and successfully complete this course. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
