    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/572": {
      "title": "WS - Spring Term INTERNSHIP - IT and AV Events Support Tech",
      "description": "WS - Spring Term INTERNSHIP - IT and AV Events Support Tech. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. EVENTS A/V and IT Support Tech Intern Division: Academic Affairs Department: Career Pathways Experience: Entry Level Job Code: GL Code: Supervisor of Student Employee(s): Charles Cable/ Angela Lockhart FWS, IWS, or Grant Funded: ☒ FWS, ☒ IWS, ☒ Grant Funded Avg. Hours/Week: ☐ 1-5, ☒ 6-10, ☒ 11-15, ☒ 16-20 Assist with the coordination and execution of campus events by supporting IT staff and event organizers with basic A/V and technology setup, event support, and equipment handling. This student position provides an opportunity to gain hands-on experience in event operations, technology, customer service, and live production while working under the guidance and supervision of experienced IT staff. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Assist with the setup, operation, and teardown of A/V and IT equipment for campus events under the direction of IT staff or event supervisors. – C, TW, P, T Assist with monitoring A/V equipment during live events , including microphones, projectors, sound systems, and other A/V accessories, and notify IT staff of issues as they arise. – C, TW, P, T Provide basic on-site event support by assisting event staff and participants with routine technology needs and referring technical issues to IT staff or supervisors when additional assistance is needed. – C, TW, CT, P, T Communicate with event staff, faculty, and IT supervisors regarding event needs, schedules, equipment requests, and issues, with guidance from assigned supervisors. – C, TW, P Assist with inventory, equipment maintenance, and storage by helping organize, transport, clean, and properly store equipment according to established procedures. – C, P, T Follow established safety and equipment-handling procedures and seek assistance from supervisors when unsure about proper procedures or equipment use. – P, T Represent the university professionally when interacting with event guests, participants, faculty, staff, and other members of the campus community. – P, C, TW Learn and follow established IT and event support procedures while developing familiarity with A/V equipment, event technology, and customer service practices. – C, P, T Work as part of the event support team by completing assigned tasks, following supervisor direction, and communicating questions or concerns as needed. – C, TW, P Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Qualifications: Entry level position In the following sections check all boxes that apply to your job. Computer Skills: ☒ Word, ☒ Excel, ☒ PowerPoint, ☐ Canva, ☒ Social Media & New Technology, ☐ Other: _________________________ Other Skills: ☒ Attention to detail, ☒ Strong active listening abilities, ☐ Public speaking, ☒ Written & verbal communication, ☒ Customer focused, ☒ Willingness to learn new things Work Schedule: ☒ Su ___ to ___; ☒ M ___ to ___; ☒ T ___ to ___; ☒ W ___ to ___; ☒ R ___ to ___; ☒ F ___ to ___; ☒ Sa ___ to ___; ☒ Hours vary depending on workload (Check days that apply, insert hours if set, otherwise, check “Hours vary depending on workload”.) Work Conditions: ☒ Heat, ☒ Cold, ☐ Odors/Smoke, ☐ Toxic Agents, ☐ Dust, ☐ Machinery, ☒ Light Intensity, ☒ Noise, ☐ Vibrations, ☐ Wetness, ☐ Humidity, ☐ Electrical Currents, ☐ Other: _________________________ Physical Demands: ☒ Keyboarding, ☒ Reaching/Handling, ☒ Stooping/Kneeling, ☒ Crouching/Crawling, ☐ Pushing up to ___ lbs., ☐ Pulling up to ___ lbs., ☒ Lifting up to 50 lbs., ☒ Carrying up to 50 lbs., ☐ Climbing, ☐ Balancing, ☐ Other: _________________________ Number of Positions: Pay Rate: [Leave Blank] Location: Building: ARM, Room #: 017 Additional Comments: Student must work a minimum of 80 hours in the semester. Student must enroll concurrently into CVL 