    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/575": {
      "title": "WS - Spring Term INTERNSHIP - Appalachian Pregnancy Care Center (APCC) Administrative Operations Assistant - FWS",
      "description": "WS - Spring Term INTERNSHIP - Appalachian Pregnancy Care Center (APCC) Administrative Operations Assistant - FWS. Department: FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. INTERNSHIP: Appalachian Pregnancy Care Center (APCC) Administrative Operations Assistant - FWS Division: Academic Affairs Department: Career Pathways Experience: Entry-level Job Code: FWSINTAPCCAO Ellucian: FWS INT APCC Admin Ops Supervisor/Reports To: Kay Hammond (APCC)/Angela Lockhart (UPIKE) Location: Off Campus 118 Loraine Street | Pikeville, KY (Walkable from UPIKE) The Administrative Operations Intern will support the daily functions of the center by optimizing office workflows, managing digital information, and enhancing communication strategies. This role is ideal for students looking to apply business theory, IT skills, and communication strategies within a mission-driven nonprofit environment. Organization Description: The Appalachian Pregnancy Care Center offers a comprehensive system of support and service for women experiencing unplanned pregnancies and their newborns. It provides necessary pre- and post-natal education resources and helps new mothers avoid the pitfalls that often accompany an unplanned or unwanted pregnancy. APCC connects clients with a broad-based network of support agencies in their community and helps mothers make positive choices involving their and their babies’ health. APCC counsels the mothers about financial and educational options and helps them maintain stability, working with the entire family unit. Internship Responsibilities and Career Competencies: Data and Records Management: Maintain and audit client/donor databases; ensure digital filing systems are organized and secure. (T, CT) Digital Communications: Draft, update, and manage media content to increase community awareness. (C, CSD) Process Optimization: Propose tech-based solutions to optimize office workflows (e.g., intake forms, supply tracking). (T, CT, CSD) Vendor and Donor Relations: Assist in coordinating logistics for fundraising events; communicate professionally with community partners and vendors. (P, C, L) Resource Coordination: Assist with organization of office and client supplies. (CTR, CT) Team Collaboration: Participate in staff meetings and collaborate on center-wide projects. (T, P, C) Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Qualifications: A current UPIKE student with interest/major/minor in Business Management, Communications, Marketing, Information Technology, or a related field. Other Skills: Attention to detail, strong active listening abilities, written & verbal communication, customer focused, willingness to learn new things, organizational efficiency, flexibility with daily tasks. Focus on confidentiality. Proficiency in Microsoft 365 or Google Workspace. Experience with Canva is a plus. Work Schedule: Tu-F 10am-4pm, some events that are on weekends and/or outside of these hours. Hours will be pre-determined upon communication between intern and supervisor. Physical Demands: Keyboarding, Reaching/Handling, Stooping/Kneeling, Lifting/Carrying, Walking moderate distances Number of Positions: 1-2 Pay Rate: Beginning at $8.75/hour Location: 118 Loraine Street | Pikeville, KY (walkable from UPIKE) Additional Comments: Student must work a minimum of 80 hours in the semester. Student must enroll concurrently into CVL 401: Integrated Internship Experience and successfully complete this course. Student must work a minimum of 80 hours in the semester. Student must enroll concurrently into CVL 401: Integrated Internship Experience and successfully complete this course. Upon hire, the intern must register for the Internship course. To receive course credit, students will complete assignments concurrently with internship work. Students are required to work a total minimum of 80 hours and will eligible for the following credit hours: 80-119 hours of work + course completion = 2 credit hours; 120-159 hours of work + course completion = 3 credit hours; 160-199 hours of work + course completion = 4 credit hours; 200-239 hours of work + course completion = 5 credit hours; 240+ hours of work = 6 credit hours. Summer interns in this position cannot exceed 40 hours of work per week. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/576": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant. Department: KYCOM Student Affairs. Full-Time. The University of Pikeville (UPIKE) is seeking an Administrative Assistant to provide comprehensive administrative, clerical, and logistical support to the Kentucky College of Osteopathic Medicine (KYCOM) Office of Student Affairs and Academic Excellence. This position will support the Associate Dean of Student Affairs and Academic Excellence team, and KYCOM students while helping ensure the efficient day-to-day operation of the office. Responsibilities: Provide daily administrative and operational support to the Associate Dean and the Office of Student Affairs and Academic Excellence. Process and maintain purchase orders, check requests, expense reports, and student organization budgets. Assist with the planning, preparation, and execution of major KYCOM events, including Orientation, the White Coat Ceremony, Commencement, and other student-focused programs. Coordinate venue reservations, catering, supply orders, and other logistical needs for student organization activities and departmental events. Maintain confidential student and departmental records in accordance with University policies and applicable privacy requirements. Maintain office supplies, submit facility work orders, and manage commonly used administrative forms and documents. Communicate professionally with students, faculty, staff, vendors, and other internal and external stakeholders. Maintain positive working relationships with vendors and campus partners. Operate standard office equipment and utilize computers, multifunction printers/copiers, phone systems, and administrative software. Perform other duties as assigned. Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent required; Associate degree or higher preferred. Previous administrative experience in higher education, a professional school, or another post-secondary academic environment preferred. Proficiency with standard computer software, office technology, and administrative applications, with the ability and willingness to learn new technologies, systems, and processes. Strong organizational skills with exceptional attention to detail. Strong interpersonal, communication, and customer service skills. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Ability to work independently with minimal supervision while collaborating effectively as part of a team. Demonstrated commitment to confidentiality, discretion, professionalism, and sound judgment. Important Notes: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 10/14/2026 will be given priority consideration. Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please, specifically address the qualifications, competencies and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, copies of their transcripts, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/577": {
      "title": "Student Success Advisor",
      "description": "Student Success Advisor. Department: Student Success. Full-Time. The University of Pikeville (UPIKE), the Leading University in Central Appalachia is actively seeking applications for the full time position of Student Success Advisor. The Student Success Advisor is expected to promote academic, personal, and social/emotional success. The Student Success Advisor is also tasked with providing appropriate academic and intermediary support to incoming freshmen and transfer students with regards to all aspects of the student’s life. Advisors will provide comprehensive testing for first-time students, track student outcomes, administer the freshman and transfer advising process, provide advising and retention training to faculty and staff, as well as provide services and support for at-risk and underserved populations. Responsibilities: Provide holistic, proactive academic advising for all first-time students, focusing on incoming freshmen and new transfer students. Ensure awareness of student services available on campus and general University policies and procedures. Focus on implementing specific strategies to assist students with academic deficiencies and those with personal and/or family issues that affect their ability to persist. Assist the Director with coordination of student services functions and work with faculty and staff to increase retention. Coordinate student evaluations during the summer orientation sessions (GROWL). If needs are identified, work with faculty to find possible learning solutions or technology to assist students as they overcome these obstacles. Administer the College Student Inventory to incoming freshmen. Coordinates with the Disability Services Coordinator to arrange necessary accommodations for individual students. Make referrals to appropriate departments, including Student Success, Student Affairs, Registrar, Business Office, Financial Aid, ACE, Disability Resource Center, etc. and monitor progress and resolutions. Maintain confidential records regarding interactions with students in accordance with FERPA Regulations. Prepare weekly and/or monthly reports regarding advising, programming, professional development, and evaluation and assessment of students. Assist with What’s Up Wednesdays, Motivational Mondays, Ask an Advisor sessions, and other student retention initiatives. Monitor student attendance and academic progress for students on academic probation. Plan and teach First Year Studies courses as needed. Engage in professional development opportunities as provided. Other duties as assigned. Education/Skill Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Education or related field. Master’s degree preferred. Must be student oriented and have a compassionate nature with the ability to be empathetic to student needs. Three years of experience in a student services/advising role is preferred. Experience with helping at-risk students in a university environment is preferred. Knowledge and experience with student success factors in higher education. Ability to work in a fast paced, collaborative environment. Ability to creatively solve student issues in a timely manner. Possess a valid driver’s license and a clear driving record with the ability to drive a 12-passenger van as permitted by the university. Important Notes: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 10/14/2026 will be given priority consideration. Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please, specifically address the qualifications, competencies and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, copies of their transcripts, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/578": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor of Biomedical Science",
      "description": "Open Rank Professor of Biomedical Science. Department: College of Arts and Sciences. Full-Time. The University of Pikeville (UPIKE) is seeking applicants for a full-time, nine-month, non-tenure-track Open-Rank Faculty position in Biomedical Science (Anatomy and Physiology), starting in January 2027. The position will focus on providing dynamic teaching and support for the University’s Biomedical Science program, as well as a commitment to the University’s mission as a school of opportunity. This faculty’s primary responsibility will be to teach biomedical science courses at all levels, with a focus on preparing students who intend to pursue study in a medical field. Applicants must demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching in a small university setting and possess the ability to work effectively with others in a collegial environment dedicated to student learning. Rank and salary will be based on qualifications. An ideal applicant will have a background and interest in human anatomy and physiology and display a passion for teaching excellence. The position’s teaching responsibilities will include biomedical science courses for majors and non-majors, as well as courses to support our health sciences programs. Courses include Anatomy and Physiology I and II for both majors and non-majors, as well as Neurobiology and other courses appropriate to the candidate’s specific expertise. The position also requires advising students, providing service to the University community, assisting with departmental activities, and continuing scholarly growth and development. As part of scholarly growth and development, faculty are encouraged to engage in research projects with undergraduate students, and we ask that interested candidates submit a statement of research interest. The University of Pikeville strives to serve students by making learning accessible and affordable. One of the University’s signature initiatives is Open Educational Resources, which provides no-cost course materials and alleviates the economic burden on students and their families. The College of Arts & Sciences offers flexible delivery modes, including face-to-face, hybrid, and online options for courses and programs. The College seeks candidates committed to the values of educational access, flexibility, innovative teaching, and active learning. Qualifications: Education: A terminal graduate degree in biomedical science or a related discipline is required. Applicants with ABD status and those within one year of completing their degree will also be considered. Experience : Demonstrated experience in teaching biomedical science courses at the undergraduate level is strongly desired. Professionalism : Ability to work effectively and professionally with students and Important Notes: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 10/16/2026 will be given priority consideration. Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please specifically address the qualifications, competencies, and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living, and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check and, when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, copies of their transcripts, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/579": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor of Biomedical Science (Anatomy & Physiology)",
      "description": "Open Rank Professor of Biomedical Science (Anatomy & Physiology). Department: College of Arts and Sciences. Full-Time. The University of Pikeville (UPIKE) is seeking a full-time, nine-month, non-tenure-track Open Rank Professor of Biomedical Science (Anatomy and Physiology) to join the College of Arts & Sciences beginning in January 2027. The successful candidate will provide engaging, student-centered instruction within UPIKE’s Biomedical Science program, with a primary focus on anatomy, physiology, and related biomedical sciences. This position supports students preparing for careers and advanced study in medicine and other health professions and requires a strong commitment to teaching excellence, student success, and the University’s mission as a school of opportunity. The ideal candidate will demonstrate expertise and interest in human anatomy and physiology, a passion for undergraduate teaching, and the ability to work collaboratively within a collegial academic environment. Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate biomedical science courses for majors and non-majors, including Anatomy and Physiology I and II. Teach Neurobiology and additional courses aligned with the candidate’s area of expertise and departmental needs. Provide instruction that supports students preparing for medical, health sciences, and other professional programs. Develop and deliver engaging, evidence-based instruction using active-learning and innovative teaching strategies. Teach courses in face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online formats as needed. Advise and mentor undergraduate students regarding academic progress, career preparation, and professional or graduate education. Participate in departmental, college, and University service activities. Assist with departmental initiatives, curriculum development, assessment, and other academic activities. Maintain continued scholarly growth and professional development within the discipline. Engage undergraduate students in research and scholarly activities when appropriate. Support the University’s commitment to educational access and affordability, including the use and development of Open Educational Resources when appropriate. Collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, and students to support student learning and the mission of the University. Perform other duties as assigned. Education and Experience: Terminal graduate degree in Biomedical Science, Anatomy, Physiology, or a closely related discipline required. Applicants who are ABD or within one year of completing the required terminal degree will also be considered. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching and student learning. Ability to work effectively and professionally with students, faculty, staff, and other members of the University community. Strong communication, interpersonal, and collaborative skills. Commitment to educational access, innovative teaching, active learning, and student success. Previous experience teaching biomedical science, anatomy, physiology, or related courses at the undergraduate level preferred. Experience teaching Anatomy and Physiology I and II preferred. Experience teaching students preparing for medical, health professions, or other graduate and professional programs preferred. Experience utilizing active-learning strategies and innovative instructional approaches preferred. Experience teaching in multiple delivery formats, including face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online courses preferred. Experience involving undergraduate students in research or scholarly activities preferred. Application Requirements: Please submit the following materials with your application: Letter of interest. Current curriculum vitae (CV). Statement of teaching philosophy. Statement of research interests, including how undergraduate students may be involved in research or scholarly activities. Important Notes: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 10/16/2026 will be given priority consideration. Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please specifically address the qualifications, competencies, and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living, and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check and, when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age, or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, copies of their transcripts, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/580": {
      "title": "Director of Academic Progress",
      "description": "Director of Academic Progress. Department: Tanner College Dental Medicine. Full-Time. The Director of Academic Progress supports the Tanner College of Dental Medicine (TCDM) by analyzing student academic performance data, managing academic records and operations, and providing reports and recommendations that support student progression, faculty decision-making, accreditation, and continuous quality improvement. The position collects, analyzes, and interprets academic performance data across TCDM’s accelerated three-year DMD curriculum, including course and competency assessments, commercial board-readiness examinations and question banks, and performance on the Integrated National Board Dental Examination (INBDE). The Director prepares reports for faculty, the Committee on Academic Performance and Standards (CAPS), and College leadership and develops institutional evaluations and related documentation supporting students’ applications for postdoctoral training, licensure, and scholarships. The Director also manages key academic operations and records for the Office of Academic Affairs and works collaboratively with faculty, College leadership, Student Affairs, the Registrar, and other University partners to ensure the accuracy, consistency, and integrity of academic information. Responsibilities: Analyze examination, course, and competency performance across the three-year DMD curriculum and prepare reports for faculty, CAPS, College leadership, and continuous quality improvement initiatives. Track and analyze indicators of INBDE readiness, including course grades, competency examination results, commercial readiness assessments, and question bank utilization and performance. Serve as the liaison between the Office of Academic Affairs and commercial assessment and question bank vendors, including account management, utilization reporting, and vendor communication. Monitor the progress of students placed on academic support, remediation, or probationary plans and maintain associated records and status reports. Prepare academic progress reports and supporting documentation for CAPS and the Associate Dean of Academic Affairs. Meet individually with students regarding academic progress, INBDE preparation, and completion of readiness benchmarks in coordination with course directors and student support services. Oversee grade, attendance, and academic standing functions within learning management and assessment systems, including ExamSoft®. Ensure the accurate and timely transfer of student performance data across academic platforms, assessment systems, and grading systems. Provide support and guidance to students and faculty regarding academic and assessment systems. Compile materials and prepare institutional evaluations, dean’s letters, and related documentation supporting applications to postdoctoral programs, licensure boards, external scholarships, and other professional opportunities. Ensure student evaluations and related documentation are prepared in accordance with College policy and applicable confidentiality requirements. Prepare and analyze data for the ADEA Survey of Dental School Seniors, internal course and program evaluations, and other student outcome assessments. Present student outcomes and assessment findings to College leadership as appropriate. Collaborate with the Director of Institutional Research and Effectiveness to support dental education research, program evaluation, institutional effectiveness, and continuous quality improvement. Design, develop, and maintain data collection, aggregation, and reporting tools, including Microsoft Excel workbooks, dashboards, and structured data transfers. Prepare and maintain data and documentation supporting CODA accreditation, self-study activities, institutional reporting, and other regulatory or accreditation requirements. Coordinate academic operations, including course scheduling, room assignments, academic calendars, examination logistics, and distribution of instructional materials. Collaborate with course directors and faculty to support effective curriculum delivery and academic scheduling. Maintain academic records, policies, procedures, and other documentation for the Office of Academic Affairs. Coordinate academic meetings, committees, and events, including preparation and distribution of agendas, materials, and meeting minutes. Manage faculty onboarding, appointment, and credentialing documentation. Track completion of faculty onboarding requirements, assessment platform training, and faculty development activities. Provide administrative and academic support to the TCDM Dean, Associate Deans for Academic Affairs and Clinical Affairs, faculty, and other College leadership as needed. Collaborate with Student Affairs, the Registrar, and TCDM administrative staff to ensure the accuracy and consistency of student academic data across the College and University. Maintain the confidentiality and security of sensitive student, academic, and personnel information in accordance with FERPA, University policy, and other applicable requirements. Perform other duties as assigned. Education and Experience: Master’s degree in education, educational measurement, data analytics, health professions education, public health, or a related field; or a bachelor’s degree with a minimum of five years of progressively responsible experience in academic administration, assessment, or a related area within a health professions program. Experience in dental, medical, or other health professions education preferred. Familiarity with the INBDE or comparable professional licensing or board examinations preferred. Experience with commercial board-preparation resources, question banks, or competency-based assessment preferred. Familiarity with Commission on Dental Accreditation (CODA) standards or other health professions accreditation requirements preferred. Experience with ExamSoft® or comparable assessment platforms preferred. Experience with statistical software, data visualization tools, dashboards, or other reporting technologies preferred. Experience supporting academic progress, student promotion, or similar academic review committees preferred. Demonstrated proficiency in data management, analysis, and reporting. Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Excel, including formulas, pivot tables, conditional formatting, data validation, and data organization. Experience preparing academic performance reports for faculty, committees, leadership, or other administrative audiences. Experience with learning management systems, assessment platforms, and student information systems. Strong written communication skills, including the ability to prepare formal evaluations, reports, committee documentation, and professional correspondence. Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities, deadlines, records, and projects in a fast-paced academic environment. Strong interpersonal and collaborative skills with the ability to work effectively with students, faculty, administrators, staff, and external partners. Demonstrated professionalism, discretion, sound judgment, and commitment to maintaining confidentiality. Important Notes: Application review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 10/16/2026 will be given priority consideration. Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please, specifically address the qualifications, competencies and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current resume, and contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/581": {
      "title": "WS - Spring Term - INTERNSHIP – Altman Eye Center – Optometric Tech – IWS",
      "description": "WS - Spring Term - INTERNSHIP – Altman Eye Center – Optometric Tech – IWS. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. INTERNSHIP – Altman Eye Center – Optometric Tech – IWS Division: Academic Affairs Department: Career Pathways 2 Experience: Experienced Job Code: GL Code: Career Pathways 2 Supervisor of Student Employee(s): Angela Lockhart, Dr. J. Turner Altman FWS, IWS, or Grant Funded: ☐ FWS, ☐ IWS, ☒ Grant Funded Avg. Hours/Week: ☐ 1-5, ☐ 6-10, ☒ 11-15, ☐ 16-20 Total 80 hours/semester Altman Eye Center, Pikeville Location | 147 Hibbard St | Pikeville, KY 41501 Altman Eye Center in Pikeville, KY is a premier optometry practice founded by Dr. J. Turner Altman, offering advanced eye care, state-of-the-art technology, and a curated boutique optical experience. Care involves routine comprehensive eye exams, diabetic-related eye evaluations, and urgent care for eye diseases such as glaucoma and macular degeneration. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: · Working patient up for eye exam. (C, P, CSD, CTR, T) · Getting patient history prior to eye exam. (C, P, CSD, T) · Providing necessary testing to get patient ready for exam. (C, P, CSD, CT, T) · Assisting the optometrists during exam, as needed. (CSD, P, TW) · Helping patients in choosing frames, taking measurements, and adjusting glasses. (C, TW, P, CSD, CT, CTR) · Calling patients for various reasons, such as to schedule, confirm, and reschedule appointments. (C, T) · Other duties shared among employees, such as organizing and light cleaning. (TW, P) Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Qualifications: · Enrolled full-time and in good standing at UPIKE. · Interest in optometry as a career. · Students with coursework, experience, or academic interest in biomedical sciences. · Willingness to carry oneself professionally in actions and appearance while in the workplace. Preferred: Biology, biomed, or similar pre-optometry pathways with demonstrated prior knowledge, education, skills, or experience related to the work. In the following sections check all boxes that apply to your job. Computer Skills: ☒ Word, ☒ Excel, ☐ PowerPoint, ☒ Canva, ☒ Social Media & New Technology, ☒ Other: _________________________ Other Skills: ☒ Attention to detail, ☒ Strong active listening abilities, ☐ Public speaking, ☒ Written & verbal communication, ☒ Customer focused, ☒ Willingness to learn new things Work Schedule: ☐ Su ___ to ___; ☐ M ___ to ___; ☐ T ___ to ___; ☐ W ___ to ___; ☐ R ___ to ___; ☐ F ___ to ___; ☐ Sa ___ to ___; ☐ Ability to designate 1 or more full day per week (approx. 8 hours) to work. Work Conditions: ☐ Heat, ☐ Cold, ☐ Odors/Smoke, ☐ Toxic Agents, ☐ Dust, ☒ Machinery, ☐ Light Intensity, ☐ Noise, ☐ Vibrations, ☐ Wetness, ☐ Humidity, ☐ Electrical Currents, ☐ Other: _________________________ Physical Demands: ☒ Keyboarding, ☒ Reaching/Handling, ☒ Stooping/Kneeling, ☐ Crouching/Crawling, ☒ Pushing up to _50_ lbs., ☒ Pulling up to _50__ lbs., ☒ Lifting up to _50__ lbs., ☒ Carrying up to _50__ lbs., ☐ Climbing, ☐ Balancing, ☐ Other: _________________________ Number of Positions: 1-2 Pay Rate: [10.50/hr Location: Altman Eye Center, Pikeville Location | 147 Hibbard St | Pikeville, KY 41501 | 6065197414 Additional Comments: · Student must work a minimum of 80 hours in the semester. Student must enroll concurrently into CVL 401: Integrated Internship Experience and successfully complete this course. Student will enroll in the 2 credit hour option for this position. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/582": {
      "title": "WS - Spring Term - INTERNSHIP – First Baptist Church of Pikeville – Ministry & Administrative Asst– IWS",
      "description": "WS - Spring Term - INTERNSHIP – First Baptist Church of Pikeville – Ministry & Administrative Asst– IWS. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. INTERNSHIP – First Baptist Church of Pikeville – Ministry & Administrative Asst– IWS Division: Academic Affairs Department: Career Pathways 2 Experience: Experienced Job Code: GL Code: Career Pathways 2 IWS Supervisor of Student Employee(s): Angela Lockhart, Keenan Darby FWS, IWS, or Grant Funded: ☐ FWS, ☐ IWS, ☒ Grant Funded Avg. Hours/Week: ☒ 1-5, ☒ 6-10, ☐11-15, ☐ 16-20 Total 80 hours/semester Location: First Baptist Church of Pikeville | 126 4th Street | Pikeville, KY 41501 The Ministry & Events Internship provides a University of Pikeville student with supervised experience in planning, logistics, coordination, and organization within a church and nonprofit setting. The intern will assist staff with weekly ministry gatherings, special events, and trips serving children, middle and high school students, and college-age young adults. Reporting to Pastor Keenan Darby and working under the guidance of church staff, the intern will learn how to move an activity from an initial idea through preparation, execution, and evaluation. This opportunity develops practical skills in event planning, hospitality, administration, and teamwork while supporting the church’s mission of making disciples and serving families. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: · Event Planning: Assist with planning ministry events, retreats, camps, outreach activities, and fellowship gatherings. Help prepare timelines, task lists, schedules, and event details. (CSD, CT, TW, T) · Weekly Ministry Coordination: Help prepare rooms, materials, supplies, refreshments, and attendance resources for weekly meetings and activities. (P, T) · Trip Logistics: Assist staff with researching destinations, transportation, lodging, meals, registration deadlines, and itineraries. Help organize permission forms and participant information. (C, TW, P, CSD, CT, T) · Volunteer Coordination: Support ministry leaders in organizing volunteer assignments, communicating schedules, and preparing volunteers for their responsibilities. (C, TW, P, CTR) · Hospitality: Help create a welcoming, organized experience through registration, check-in, signage, room preparation, and assistance to participants and families. (C, TW, P, CSD, CTR, L) · Communication: Prepare staff-approved reminders, schedules, packing lists, and instructions for parents, students, volunteers, and participants. Coordinate promotional needs with the church’s communications team. (C, TW, P, CSD, CT, T) · Budgets and Supplies: Learn to estimate costs, compare options, track approved expenses, organize receipts, and maintain supplies within established budgets. (CSD, CT, T) · Event Support and Evaluation: Assist with setup, activities, cleanup, and follow-up. Participate in staff debriefs to identify improvements for future events. (C, TW, P, CSD) Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Qualifications: · Enrolled full-time and in good standing at UPIKE. · Demonstrated prior experience, education, or advanced skill in business administration/management, communications, education, religious studies, or related work appropriate to the responsibilities of this position. Preferred Qualifications: · Students with coursework, experience, or academic interest in event planning, hospitality, nonprofit administration, or church ministry are encouraged to apply. · Strong organizational skills, dependability, attention to detail, and a willingness to learn. · Ability to communicate respectfully with children, students, parents, volunteers, and staff. · Willingness to receive feedback, work as part of a team, and follow through on assigned tasks. · Basic proficiency with email, documents, spreadsheets, and digital calendars. · Must affirm agreement with the church’s statement of faith and maintain conduct consistent with those beliefs throughout the internship. · Must complete the church’s required background screening and child-protection training before working with minors and follow all supervision and safety policies. In the following sections check all boxes that apply to your job. Computer Skills: ☒ Word, ☒ Excel, ☒ PowerPoint, ☒ Canva, ☒ Social Media & New Technology, ☒ Other: _________________________ Other Skills: ☒ Attention to detail, ☒ Strong active listening abilities, ☐ Public speaking, ☒ Written & verbal communication, ☒ Customer focused, ☒ Willingness to learn new things Work Schedule: ☐ Su ___ to ___; ☐ M ___ to ___; ☐ T ___ to ___; ☐ W ___ to ___; ☐ R ___ to ___; ☐ F ___ to ___; ☐ Sa ___ to ___; ☒ Other: Preferred schedule: 1 hour Sunday morning, 1 ½ hours Wednesday Night, and 2 ½ hours a week in office that works with intern’s schedule during the 9am-3pm window. Work Conditions: ☐ Heat, ☐ Cold, ☐ Odors/Smoke, ☐ Toxic Agents, ☐ Dust, ☐ Machinery, ☐ Light Intensity, ☒ Noise, ☐ Vibrations, ☐ Wetness, ☐ Humidity, ☐ Electrical Currents, ☐ Other: _________________________ Physical Demands: ☒ Keyboarding, ☒ Reaching/Handling, ☒ Stooping/Kneeling, ☐ Crouching/Crawling, ☒ Pushing up to _50_ lbs., ☒ Pulling up to _50__ lbs., ☒ Lifting up to _50__ lbs., ☒ Carrying up to _50__ lbs., ☐ Climbing, ☐ Balancing, ☐ Other: _________________________ Number of Positions: 1 Pay Rate: 10.50/hr Location: First Baptist Church of Pikeville | 126 4th Street | Pikeville, KY 41501 | 6064328113 Additional Comments: · Student must work a minimum of 80 hours in the semester. Student must enroll concurrently into CVL 401: Integrated Internship Experience and successfully complete this course. Student will enroll in the 2 credit hour option for this position. · By the end of the internship, the student should be able to develop an event plan, organize logistics and schedules, communicate with participants and volunteers, track basic expenses, and evaluate an event’s effectiveness. The intern will gain practical experience applicable to ministry, event coordination, hospitality, and nonprofit operations. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/583": {
      "title": "WS - Spring Term - INTERNSHIP – First Baptist Church of Pikeville – Media & Communications– IWS",
      "description": "WS - Spring Term - INTERNSHIP – First Baptist Church of Pikeville – Media & Communications– IWS. Department: IWS/FWS - Student Employment. Student Worker. INTERNSHIP – First Baptist Church of Pikeville – Media & Communications– IWS Division: Academic Affairs Department: Career Pathways 2 Experience: Experienced Job Code: GL Code: Career Pathways 2 IWS Supervisor of Student Employee(s): Angela Lockhart, Shawn Dobbins FWS, IWS, or Grant Funded: ☐ FWS, ☐ IWS, ☒ Grant Funded Avg. Hours/Week: ☒ 1-5, ☒ 6-10, ☐11-15, ☐ 16-20 Total 80 hours/semester Location: First Baptist Church of Pikeville | 126 4th Street | Pikeville, KY 41501 The Media & Communications Internship provides a University of Pikeville student with practical experience creating digital and printed communications in a ministry and nonprofit setting. Reporting to Pastor Shawn Dobbins and working under the guidance of church staff, the intern will learn to produce social media content, worship graphics, videos, and printed materials for weekly services and special events. The intern will help communicate the church’s mission, strengthen its online presence, and connect church members and the surrounding community with its ministries. This is a supervised learning opportunity designed to develop creative skills, professional experience, and a portfolio of completed work. Responsibilities and Career Competencies: · Social Media: Help plan, write, design, and schedule approved posts that highlight church ministries, share stories, promote events, and encourage engagement. (CSD, C, P, T) · Worship Graphics: Assist with sermon series artwork, presentation slides, announcements, and other visual materials for weekly worship services. (C, P, T) · Video and Photography: Learn to capture and edit photos, short videos, ministry stories, sermon clips, and event promotions. (CSD, C, CT, CTR, T) · AI Tools: Utilize provided AI tools and other AI tools as needed. (CSD, T) · Printed Communications: Help create and proofread bulletins, flyers, invitations, brochures, signs, and other materials for services and special events. (CSD, C, CT, P, T) · Brand and Mission: Learn to use consistent colors, fonts, imagery, and messaging so the church’s communications clearly reflect its identity and mission. (CSD, C, T) · Communication Planning: Work with staff to maintain a content calendar, gather ministry information, and meet production deadlines. (CSD, C, L, P, TW) · Audience Engagement: Help adapt messages for church members, guests, and the wider community, and review basic engagement results to improve future content. (C, CT, CTR, P) Competencies/Skills: Communication (C), Teamwork (TW), Professionalism (P), Career & Self Development (CSD), Critical Thinking (CT), Community Transformation (CTR), Leadership (L), Technology (T) Qualifications: · Enrolled full-time and in good standing at UPIKE. · Demonstrated prior knowledge in Communication, Marketing, Film and Media Arts, or related work appropriate to the responsibilities of this position. Preferred Qualifications: · Students with coursework, experience, or academic interest in social media, graphic design, photography, video production, or nonprofit communications are encouraged to apply. · Basic writing and computer skills, attention to detail, and a willingness to learn creative software. · Must affirm agreement with the church’s statement of faith and maintain conduct consistent with those beliefs throughout the internship. · Dependability, initiative, and the ability to meet deadlines and receive constructive feedback. · Willingness to support and accurately represent the church’s mission, beliefs, and ministry priorities. · Good judgment when handling personal information, photographs, and ministry stories. · Familiarity with Canva, Adobe Creative Cloud, or video editing tools is helpful but not required. In the following sections check all boxes that apply to your job. Computer Skills: ☒ Word, ☒ Excel, ☒ PowerPoint, ☒ Canva, ☒ Social Media & New Technology, ☒ Other: _________________________ Other Skills: ☒ Attention to detail, ☒ Strong active listening abilities, ☐ Public speaking, ☒ Written & verbal communication, ☒ Customer focused, ☒ Willingness to learn new things Work Schedule: ☐ Su ___ to ___; ☐ M ___ to ___; ☐ T ___ to ___; ☐ W ___ to ___; ☐ R ___ to ___; ☐ F ___ to ___; ☐ Sa ___ to ___; ☒ Other: Preferred schedule: 1 hour Sunday morning, and 4 hours a week in office that works with intern’s schedule during the 9am-3pm window. Work Conditions: ☐ Heat, ☐ Cold, ☐ Odors/Smoke, ☐ Toxic Agents, ☐ Dust, ☐ Machinery, ☐ Light Intensity, ☒ Noise, ☐ Vibrations, ☐ Wetness, ☐ Humidity, ☐ Electrical Currents, ☐ Other: _________________________ Physical Demands: ☒ Keyboarding, ☒ Reaching/Handling, ☒ Stooping/Kneeling, ☐ Crouching/Crawling, ☒ Pushing up to _50_ lbs., ☒ Pulling up to _50__ lbs., ☒ Lifting up to _50__ lbs., ☒ Carrying up to _50__ lbs., ☐ Climbing, ☐ Balancing, ☐ Other: _________________________ Number of Positions: 1 Pay Rate:10.50/hr Location: First Baptist Church of Pikeville | 126 4th Street | Pikeville, KY 41501 | 6064328113 Additional Comments: · Student must work a minimum of 80 hours in the semester. Student must enroll concurrently into CVL 401: Integrated Internship Experience and successfully complete this course. Student will enroll in the 2 credit hour option for this position. · Shawn Dobbins (site supervisor) will provide overall direction, with church staff offering project assignments, training, and feedback. Projects will reflect the student’s experience and learning goals, with increasing responsibility as skills develop. Public-facing content will receive staff approval before publication. · By the end of the internship, the student should demonstrate growth in content creation, visual storytelling, communication planning, consistent branding, and collaboration within a nonprofit organization. Approved projects may be included in a professional portfolio. Application Notes: Resumes and applications will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/584": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty-Medical Biochemistry",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty-Medical Biochemistry. Department: KYCOM Basic Science. Adjunct Faculty. The University of Pikeville seeks adjunct faculty who are dedicated to excellence in teaching and student learning. This position would be directly responsible for online/remote teaching in medical biochemistry. Responsibilites: Responsible for teaching medical biochemistry. Preparation of lectures, lecture notes, learning objectives, PowerPoint slides, exam questions, and syllabi offered on accelerated 8-week terms and delivered asynchronously through Canvas Learning Management System. Participates in and recommends curriculum development and evaluation. Fostering an engaging learning environment with innovative pedagogical practices. Provides mentoring and guidance to students. Other duties as assigned. Requirements: Must have terminal degree as required, PhD. On-line teaching experience Faculty Expectations: Note that the University of Pikeville recognizes that effective educators are themselves life-long learners. Part-time faculty members are encouraged to attend our professional development workshops whenever possible to improve use of educational technology, determine ways to better engage students, and reflect on methods to create the most effective environment for student growth. Positions are available in the spring, summer, and fall semesters. Review of applications occur as needed. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, copies of their transcripts, a teaching philosophy statement, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/585": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Microbiology",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Microbiology. Department: KYCOM Basic Science. Adjunct Faculty. The University of Pikeville is seeking a qualified Adjunct Professor of Microbiology to provide high-quality instruction in an online learning environment for the Master of Science in Biomedical Science program. This position is responsible for developing and delivering engaging, asynchronous coursework, supporting student learning, and contributing to curriculum development and continuous improvement. Responsibilities: Deliver online instruction in Microbiology through accelerated eight-week courses using the Canvas Learning Management System. Develop and maintain course materials, including lectures, lecture notes, learning objectives, PowerPoint presentations, syllabi, and assessments. Design and administer examinations and other assessments to evaluate student learning and achievement of course objectives. Create an engaging and supportive online learning environment through innovative instructional methods and effective teaching practices. Provide academic guidance, mentorship, and timely feedback to students. Participate in curriculum development, review, and evaluation to maintain instructional quality and program effectiveness. Collaborate with program leadership and faculty to support academic goals and student success. Perform other duties as assigned. Requirement Qualifications: Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in Microbiology or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated knowledge and expertise in Microbiology. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work independently and effectively in a remote instructional environment. Proficiency with technology and digital tools used in online education. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience teaching in an online or asynchronous learning environment. Experience using Canvas or a comparable Learning Management System. Experience teaching accelerated courses at the graduate level. Demonstrated ability to develop engaging online instructional materials and assessments. Faculty Expectations: Note that the University of Pikeville recognizes that effective educators are themselves life-long learners. Part-time faculty members are encouraged to attend our professional development workshops whenever possible to improve use of educational technology, determine ways to better engage students, and reflect on methods to create the most effective environment for student growth. Positions are available in the spring, summer, and fall semesters. Review of applications occur as needed. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, copies of their transcripts, a teaching philosophy statement, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/587": {
      "title": "General Dentistry Faculty and Director of the Advanced Placement International Dental Program",
      "description": "General Dentistry Faculty and Director of the Advanced Placement International Dental Program. Department: Tanner College Dental Medicine. Full-Time. The University of Pikeville's Tanner College of Dental Medicine (TCDM) invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track faculty position as the Director of the Advanced Placement International Dental (APID) Program. This position serves as a general dentist faculty member responsible for teaching general dentistry in classroom, preclinical, and clinical settings within the Doctor of Dental Medicine (DMD) curriculum. In addition to faculty responsibilities, the Director provides leadership and oversight of the APID Program, supporting the academic success, integration, and professional development of internationally educated dentists. Working collaboratively with academic leadership, faculty, and University partners, the Director coordinates program activities, monitors student progress, provides academic advising, and supports curriculum development and assessment. The Director also contributes to TCDM through teaching, scholarship, faculty development, accreditation, and institutional service. Responsibilities: Provide instruction, demonstration, supervision, and feedback to students in classroom, laboratory, simulation, and clinical settings. Develop and deliver learning activities and assessments that support an integrated, competency-based dental curriculum. Participate in course development, curriculum review, faculty calibration, student assessment, grading, remediation, and continuous improvement initiatives. Provide leadership and oversight of the APID Program, coordinating academic activities and educational experiences with academic leadership and faculty. Facilitate the orientation, transition, and integration of internationally educated dentists into the TCDM educational environment. Serve as the primary faculty resource for APID students, providing academic advising, mentoring, and individualized support. Monitor student academic progress, identify areas of concern, and coordinate appropriate interventions and remediation. Collaborate with course directors and faculty to integrate APID students into classroom, laboratory, simulation, and clinical education. Work with admissions, student affairs, academic support, and other University departments to support student success. Assist in developing and maintaining APID Program policies, procedures, academic processes, and student records. Communicate program expectations, academic requirements, and educational processes to prospective, admitted, and enrolled students. Evaluate program effectiveness, analyze student performance and outcomes, and recommend improvements. Support accreditation preparation, institutional assessment, strategic planning, and continuous quality improvement. Serve as a faculty resource regarding the educational needs of internationally educated dentists and students from diverse backgrounds. Support student development in clinical reasoning, professional communication, clinical readiness, scholarship, and service. Maintain scholarly activity and professional development consistent with faculty appointment and rank. Participate in faculty meetings, committees, faculty development, and other institutional activities. Perform other duties as assigned in support of the College's educational mission. Education Requirements: Doctor of Dental Medicine (DMD), Doctor of Dental Surgery (DDS), or equivalent dental degree from a CODA-accredited institution, or an equivalent dental degree. Education Preferred: Advanced training, graduate education, or specialty education in dentistry or dental education. Experience Required: Demonstrated experience in dental education, teaching, or academic dentistry, including working with students in academic or clinical educational settings. Clinical dentistry experience and/or advanced training or expertise in a dental specialty. Kentucky dental license or eligibility for a Kentucky dental license or faculty-limited license. Strong interpersonal, communication, organizational, and collaborative skills. Demonstrated commitment to student success, academic excellence, and a supportive, student-centered learning environment. Experience Preferred: Experience teaching or mentoring internationally educated dentists or students from diverse educational and cultural backgrounds. Experience coordinating, directing, or supporting an advanced placement or international dental education program. The University of Pikeville offers a competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. UPIKE offers a competitive benefits package including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance, telemedicine, long term disability, tuition waivers, a 403(b)-retirement plan, and HSA, FSA, & dependent care accounts. UPIKE also offers a generous holiday schedule and paid leave program. Important Notes: Application review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 11/06/2026 will be given priority consideration. Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please, specifically address the qualifications, competencies and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, copies of their transcripts, a teaching philosophy statement, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/588": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor - Anatomy",
      "description": "Open Rank Professor - Anatomy. Department: KYCOM Basic Science. Full-Time. The University of Pikeville and Kentucky College of Osteopathic Medicine (KYCOM) is seeking an Open Rank Professor of Anatomy within the Department of Biomedical Sciences. KYCOM is ranked #2 by US News and World Report in medical schools with the most graduates practicing in rural areas and #11 in medical schools with the most graduates in practicing primary care. With nearly 550 students, faculty and staff are committed to teaching and learning, innovation, and the success of medical education. This full-time position is under the supervision of the Associate Dean of Biomedical Sciences, with direct responsibility for teaching, scholarly activity/research and service in the discipline of anatomy. Responsibilities: Teaching in one or more of the Anatomical Science courses (Language of Medicine, Cardiovascular, Pulmonary and Renal Systems, Nervous System with Head and Neck) and includes preparation of lectures, lecture notes, learning objectives, PowerPoint slides, exam questions, and syllabi. Facilitates the Integrated Case Studies in the Fall and Spring semesters. Participates in and recommends curriculum development and evaluation. Research and other scholarly activities. Provide counseling and guidance for students. Serves on assigned KYCOM, KYCO, and University of Pikeville committees. Attends Commencement, White Coat Ceremony, New Student Orientation, and University of Pikeville Opening Convocation. Participates in faculty development. Assists in the selection of students to attend KYCOM. Other duties as assigned by the KYCOM Dean. Education: Earned doctorate degree. Experience: Previous academic experience preferably at an osteopathic or allopathic medical educational program. Experience teaching face-to-face and/or online within a higher education environment. Skills and Abilities: Must have excellent verbal and written communication skills. Strong critical thinking, anticipatory problem-solving, and attention to detail are required. Ability to plan, prioritize, and organize work to complete assignments accurately and within reasonable timeframes. Ability to embrace diversity to best serve a growing higher education community. Ability to foster excellence and innovation. A history of demonstrating strong character and outstanding integrity. Must have current knowledge and skills in utilizing Microsoft Office Applications, including but not limited to Outlook, PowerPoint, Word, and Excel. Must be able to learn and utilize Learning Management Systems such as Canvas and the University's online platform and systems. Must demonstrate cooperation, courtesy, and consideration when working with the professional community, KYCOM, KYCO, and UPIKE communities, faculty, students, and the public. Must be able to work independently and as a member of a team. Alignment with the University of Pikeville and KYCOM and KYCO missions. The University of Pikeville offers a competitive salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. UPIKE offers a competitive benefits package including medical, dental, vision, and life insurance, telemedicine, long term disability, tuition waivers, a 403(b)-retirement plan, and HSA, FSA, & dependent care accounts. UPIKE also offers a generous holiday schedule and paid leave program. Application review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received on or before 11/16/2026 will be given priority consideration. Important Notes: Resume and other application materials will be reviewed to determine if you meet the required qualifications for the position. If it is determined that you meet the required qualifications, your application materials will be used to identify a top group of the most highly qualified candidates. Please, specifically address the qualifications, competencies and desired qualifications in your resume and application materials. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, copies of their transcripts, a teaching philosophy statement, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
    },
    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/589": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor in Applied Genetics",
      "description": "Adjunct Professor in Applied Genetics. Department: KYCOM Basic Science. Adjunct Faculty. The University of Pikeville is seeking a qualified Adjunct Professor of Applied Genetics to provide high-quality instruction in an online learning environment for the Master of Science in Biomedical Science program. This position is responsible for developing and delivering engaging, asynchronous coursework, supporting student learning, and contributing to curriculum development and continuous improvement. Responsibilities: Deliver online instruction in Microbiology through accelerated eight-week courses using the Canvas Learning Management System. Develop and maintain course materials, including lectures, lecture notes, learning objectives, PowerPoint presentations, syllabi, and assessments. Design and administer examinations and other assessments to evaluate student learning and achievement of course objectives. Create an engaging and supportive online learning environment through innovative instructional methods and effective teaching practices. Provide academic guidance, mentorship, and timely feedback to students. Participate in curriculum development, review, and evaluation to maintain instructional quality and program effectiveness. Collaborate with program leadership and faculty to support academic goals and student success. Perform other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in Applied Genetics. Demonstrated knowledge and expertise in Applied Genetics. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work independently and effectively in a remote instructional environment. Proficiency with technology and digital tools used in online education. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience teaching in an online or asynchronous learning environment. Experience using Canvas or a comparable Learning Management System. Experience teaching accelerated courses at the graduate level. Demonstrated ability to develop engaging online instructional materials and assessments. Faculty Expectations: Note that the University of Pikeville recognizes that effective educators are themselves life-long learners. Part-time faculty members are encouraged to attend our professional development workshops whenever possible to improve use of educational technology, determine ways to better engage students, and reflect on methods to create the most effective environment for student growth. Positions are available in the spring, summer, and fall semesters. Review of applications occur as needed. The University of Pikeville is committed to providing a safe and productive learning, living and working community. To achieve this goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. The University of Pikeville is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a diverse, broadly trained faculty and staff. The University of Pikeville does not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, color, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, national origin, age or disabilities in its programs, activities, hiring, or the admission of students. For more information about the University of Pikeville, please visit http://www.upike.edu . In addition to the application, interested applicants are requested to attach to their application a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, copies of their transcripts, a teaching philosophy statement, and the contact information for three to five professional references."
