    "https://upike.bamboohr.com/careers/591": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor in Biology/Biomedical Science (Generalist)",
      "description": "Adjunct Professor in Biology/Biomedical Science (Generalist). Department: KYCOM Basic Science. Adjunct Faculty. The University of Pikeville is seeking a qualified Adjunct Professor of Biology/Biomedical Science (Generalist) to provide high-quality instruction in an online learning environment for the Master of Science in Biomedical Science program. This position is responsible for developing and delivering engaging, asynchronous coursework, supporting student learning, and contributing to curriculum development and continuous improvement. Responsibilities: Responsible for teaching key areas of biomedical science, including cell biology, molecular biology, and biochemistry, as they relate to human health and disease (teaching Foundations in Biomedical Sciences and capstone). Describing and integrating fundamental concepts across biochemistry, cell biology, genetics, and physiology. Responsible for helping students develop a focused research question, synthesize literature, design, and execute a scholarly product, and communicate findings in both written and oral formats. Deliver online instruction in accelerated eight-week courses using the Canvas Learning Management System. Develop and maintain course materials, including lectures, lecture notes, learning objectives, PowerPoint presentations, syllabi, and assessments. Design and administer examinations and other assessments to evaluate student learning and achievement of course objectives. Create an engaging and supportive online learning environment through innovative instructional methods and effective teaching practices. Provide academic guidance, mentorship, and timely feedback to students. Participate in curriculum development, review, and evaluation to maintain instructional quality and program effectiveness. Collaborate with program leadership and faculty to support academic goals and student success. Perform other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: Ph.D. or equivalent terminal